      "<strong>v1.35.6 &mdash; Square OAuth scope set narrowed + webhook subscription degraded to non-fatal. v1.35.5&rsquo;s redirect_uri fix didn&rsquo;t resolve the <code>401 service.not_authorized</code> from Square&rsquo;s token exchange. Same identical rejection on every retry across multiple OAuth flows. The diagnostic confirmed via the consent screen rendering only 7 scopes instead of the 9 we request &mdash; Square&rsquo;s auth UI is silently dropping the two <code>DEVELOPER_APPLICATION_WEBHOOKS_*</code> scopes from user-facing consent, but the token-exchange POST still includes them in the requested scope set, triggering Square to reject the whole exchange with <code>service.not_authorized</code> because the app isn&rsquo;t app-level approved to use those partner-tier scopes.</strong> <strong>v1.35.6 isolates the issue</strong>: (1) removed <code>DEVELOPER_APPLICATION_WEBHOOKS_WRITE</code> + <code>DEVELOPER_APPLICATION_WEBHOOKS_READ</code> from <code>SQUARE_OAUTH_SCOPES</code> &mdash; back to the 7-scope set the consent UI actually surfaces. Token exchange should now succeed. (2) Webhook subscription step in the OAuth callback degraded to non-fatal &mdash; if <code>createSquareWebhookSubscription</code> throws (it will, since we&rsquo;re not requesting the scope anymore), the connect flow continues with <code>webhook_subscription_id</code> left null. The connection lands in <code>status=&quot;connected&quot;</code> with the warning stamped on <code>last_error</code> for settings-page visibility: &lsquo;Webhook subscription unavailable on this Square app. Connection works for read sync; real-time push deferred until app approval or polling fallback.&rsquo; <strong>Strategic implications</strong>: read sync via polling becomes the v1 substrate for Square instead of push webhooks. Polling fallback is a follow-up ship &mdash; for v1.35.6 the connection just doesn&rsquo;t auto-sync after the initial 90-day backfill; user can hit Re-sync manually to refresh. <strong>What this doesn&rsquo;t fix yet</strong>: real-time push notifications when a Square seller cancels/no-shows. Without webhooks Refill won&rsquo;t know about a cancellation until the next poll or manual re-sync. The proper fix is either (a) get Square to approve the app for partner-tier webhook scopes (manual support ticket process), or (b) ship a polling-based sync (~30-min cron sweeping each connected Square seller&rsquo;s next-7-day window). Banking the choice for after this debug arc closes. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/lib/schedulers/square.ts</code> (removed 2 webhook scopes from SQUARE_OAUTH_SCOPES + extended comment), <code>src/routes/api.integrations.square.oauth-callback.ts</code> (try/catch around createSquareWebhookSubscription now stamps webhook_warning to last_error instead of returning errReturn; subscription persistence conditional on success; final status=&quot;connected&quot; preserves either tier_gate OR webhook_warning), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No schema change; no new dependencies; no Worker secret changes. <strong>Debug arc retrospective</strong>: v1.35.0 (webhook scope gap) → v1.35.1 (added scopes) → v1.35.2 (defensive trim SQUARE_ENV) → v1.35.3 (SQUARE_ENV into wrangler.jsonc) → v1.35.4 (whitespace strip credentials + bubble Square error to URL) → v1.35.5 (redirect_uri in token body) → v1.35.6 (drop the over-scoped request). Each step necessary, each surfaced by the prior step&rsquo;s diagnostic improvement. The error-surfacing pattern (v1.35.4) was the unlock for every subsequent step.",
