      "<strong>v1.35.5 &mdash; Square OAuth token-exchange redirect_uri fix. v1.35.4&rsquo;s error-surfacing revealed the actual Square rejection: <code>401 { message: &quot;Not Authorized&quot;, type: &quot;service.not_authorized&quot; }</code> &mdash; not a credentials problem (those were verified clean across multiple re-paste cycles) but a missing required parameter in my token exchange body.</strong> Square&rsquo;s <code>/oauth2/token</code> spec requires <code>redirect_uri</code> to be echoed back in the POST body for <code>authorization_code</code> grants, even when the corresponding <code>/oauth2/authorize</code> URL didn&rsquo;t include redirect_uri explicitly (Square uses the registered URL from app config silently in authorize, but expects the value back during token exchange for verification). My <code>exchangeSquareCodeForToken</code> body had <code>client_id</code> + <code>client_secret</code> + <code>code</code> + <code>grant_type</code> but omitted <code>redirect_uri</code>. Square returned <code>service.not_authorized</code> for the missing field rather than a clear &lsquo;missing parameter&rsquo; error &mdash; an error-classification quirk that masked the real cause through three deploys and six debug iterations. <strong>Fix</strong>: added <code>redirect_uri: args.credentials.redirectUri</code> to the POST body in <code>exchangeSquareCodeForToken</code>. The <code>redirectUri</code> arg was already being passed in by the OAuth callback (constructed as <code>${url.origin}/api/integrations/square/oauth-callback</code>) but unused. Now sent and verified against Square&rsquo;s registered Sandbox Redirect URL. <strong>Debug arc retrospective</strong>: v1.35.0 webhook scope gap → v1.35.1 added scopes → v1.35.2 defensive trim on SQUARE_ENV value → v1.35.3 SQUARE_ENV into wrangler.jsonc (deploys were wiping the dashboard-side var) → v1.35.4 whitespace strip on credentials + bubble Square error detail to URL → v1.35.5 redirect_uri in token body. Each fix was necessary; the underlying causes were genuinely independent (scope config, defensive trim, dashboard-vs-config var persistence, error message visibility, missing required param). The token_exchange ERROR-SURFACING ship (v1.35.4) was the unlock &mdash; without it, the redirect_uri root cause would have stayed buried under the generic <code>scheduler_error=token_exchange</code> redirect URL. Architectural learning banked: <strong>any OAuth callback handler that catches errors MUST bubble the actual provider error text into the user-visible redirect URL or settings dashboard</strong>, not just emit a generic error code. The 10-minute fix took an hour because the generic code obscured the actual rejection reason. Same pattern needs to land on Mindbody / Boulevard OAuth handlers when they ship. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/lib/schedulers/square.ts</code> (add redirect_uri to body in <code>exchangeSquareCodeForToken</code> + explanatory comment), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No schema change; no new dependencies; no Worker secret changes.",
