      "<strong>v1.35.0 &mdash; Square Appointments as Refill&rsquo;s second live scheduler integration. Closes the 4-platform multi-scheduler thesis Phase 1 by hardening the connector substrate against its first divergence axis (single-global webhook URL + tenant-routing-via-payload pattern). Pre-ship: Acuity-only since v381; sales conversations stalled on &lsquo;do you support [other scheduler]?&rsquo; Post-ship: Square is the second platform live, on the same <code>emma_scheduler_connections</code> substrate, with platform-agnostic dispatch through claim writeback.</strong> <strong>Substrate divergences Square absorbs (vs Acuity-shaped today)</strong>: (1) <strong>Single global webhook URL</strong> &mdash; <code>/api/webhooks/scheduler/square</code> with no per-spa secret in the path; tenant routing happens via <code>merchant_id</code> in the payload, looked up against <code>(platform=&quot;square&quot;, platform_account_id)</code>. Mindbody / Boulevard will reuse this pattern when they ship. (2) <strong>HMAC verification scheme</strong> &mdash; SHA-256 over <code>(notification_url + raw_body)</code> concatenation, base64-encoded in <code>x-square-hmacsha256-signature</code>. Unlike Acuity&rsquo;s advisory-mode signature, Square&rsquo;s scheme is well-documented + consistent so verification is HARD-reject on mismatch. (3) <strong>30-day token + refresh flow</strong> &mdash; new <code>withFreshSquareToken</code> helper in emma-scheduler.functions.ts auto-refreshes any token within 3 days of expiry on every webhook + writeback call. (4) <strong>Subscription resource ID lifecycle</strong> &mdash; Square issues a subscription_id at create-time + requires it for delete; new <code>webhook_subscription_id</code> column on emma_scheduler_connections stores it; <code>webhook_secret</code> column overloaded to hold Square&rsquo;s per-subscription signature_key (kept the column name; Acuity rows continue using it as URL-path secret). (5) <strong>Tier-gate detection</strong> &mdash; first-sync probes <code>GET /v2/bookings</code> and surfaces &lsquo;Square Free tier detected&rsquo; on the settings page if the seller can&rsquo;t write. <code>CreateBooking</code> requires Square Appointments Plus or Premium. Free-tier sellers sync + Rescue still fires; only the claim writeback degrades with a banner explaining the upgrade need (NOT a hard disconnect). <strong>Files added</strong>: <code>src/lib/schedulers/square.ts</code> (~500 LOC connector mirroring acuity.ts shape: OAuth helpers, GET/POST API client, getSquareMerchant + probeSquareBookingsTier + listSquareBookings + getSquareBooking + createSquareBooking + upsertSquareCustomer + createSquareWebhookSubscription + deleteSquareWebhookSubscription + verifySquareWebhookSignature + parseSquareWebhookBody + squareStatusToRefillStatus); <code>src/routes/api.integrations.square.oauth-callback.ts</code> (~280 LOC OAuth callback: 5-min code exchange, connection upsert, webhook subscription registration, tier probe, backfill, status finalization &mdash; structural mirror of api.integrations.acuity.oauth-callback.ts); <code>src/routes/api.webhooks.scheduler.square.ts</code> (~330 LOC receiver: HMAC verification, merchant_id lookup, booking resolution via embedded-or-GET, upsert, trigger graph &mdash; same trigger-graph fanout as Acuity receiver into rescue dispatch + reliability recompute); <code>supabase/migrations/20260625000000_v1_35_0_square_webhook_subscription.sql</code> (adds <code>webhook_subscription_id</code> column nullable). <strong>Files extended</strong>: <code>src/server/emma-scheduler.functions.ts</code> &mdash; new <code>initiateSquareOAuth</code> server fn (mirror of initiateAcuityOAuth with sandbox/prod env switch); Square dispatch in <code>disconnectScheduler</code> (calls deleteSquareWebhookSubscription with stored subscription_id; fail-open if token revoked); Square dispatch in <code>resyncSchedulerConnection</code> (calls backfillSquareBookings); new <code>backfillSquareBookings</code> helper paginating /v2/bookings with cursor + idempotent upsert on (user_id, external_id, source); new <code>squareBookingToRow</code> + <code>withFreshSquareToken</code> exports. <code>src/server/emma-rescue.functions.ts</code> &mdash; claimRescueSlot writeback dispatch refactored from <code>acuitySource</code> boolean to <code>writeableSource</code> tagged-union ({acuity, square, null}); new Square branch (~120 LOC) that loads the rescue claimer&rsquo;s contact info, runs <code>withFreshSquareToken</code> to ensure token is current, fetches the original booking for locationId + appointmentSegments, find-or-creates the customer via upsertSquareCustomer, posts createSquareBooking with the original slot info + new customerId + idempotency key tied to the offer ID, stamps new external_id, and SPECIFICALLY detects Square Free-tier 403s to emit <code>writeback_failed: tier_blocked (Square Appointments Plus/Premium required)</code> for the Rescue dashboard to render as an upgrade prompt distinct from generic failures. Same fail-open semantics as Acuity v382 &mdash; claim stays committed even on writeback failure; the patient never gets punished for an upstream API issue. <code>src/routes/app.refill.settings.scheduler.tsx</code> &mdash; new Connect Square card in AvailablePlatforms; new <code>connectSquare</code> handler that calls initiateSquareOAuth + window.location.href to the redirect URL; &ldquo;Coming soon&rdquo; section updated (Mindbody / JaneApp / Boulevard remain queued). <strong>What this DOES NOT change</strong>: the Acuity hot path is untouched &mdash; same routes, same connector, same trigger graph. Mindbody / Boulevard / JaneApp specs were banked Jun 2 as v0.3 / v0.1 / TBD respectively but no code lands for them yet. The patient-roster import path is Acuity-specific (importAcuityClients); Square&rsquo;s customer roster is exposed via /v2/customers but the rich field-mapping into knowledge_nodes is queued for a follow-up ship &mdash; the initial backfill seeds emma_appointments without resolving patient_node_id for net-new Square sellers (matches the v381 Acuity baseline). <strong>Prerequisites for live test</strong> (not blocking ship): (1) Square Developer Console signup at developer.squareup.com/apps &mdash; create Refill app + sandbox app; (2) Cloudflare Worker secrets set: SQUARE_APP_ID, SQUARE_APP_SECRET, SQUARE_SANDBOX_APP_ID, SQUARE_SANDBOX_APP_SECRET, SQUARE_ENV (=&quot;sandbox&quot; or &quot;production&quot;); (3) migration applied via Supabase dashboard before first Square OAuth flow fires; (4) redirect URL <code>https://getrefill.app/api/integrations/square/oauth-callback</code> registered on the Square app&rsquo;s OAuth tab. <strong>Strategic anchor</strong>: per [[project-multi-scheduler-thesis]] the substrate is now genuinely platform-agnostic, not Acuity-shaped-pretending-to-be. By the time Mindbody&rsquo;s OAuth client provisioning ticket clears, the abstraction handles divergent webhook routing, divergent token lifecycles, divergent admin-override semantics, and divergent tier-gating &mdash; one connector pattern, four absorbed shapes. Boulevard&rsquo;s GraphQL substrate divergence is the only NEW axis remaining; same connector shape will hold.",
