      "<strong>v1.34.9.5 &mdash; Gap close #3: Attribution settings now actually reach dispatch. Pre-ship: <code>/app/refill/agents/attribution</code> let Karen set window-hours / auto-confirm-threshold / master-toggle, but emma-attribution.functions.ts dispatch ignored them and used a hardcoded 14-day window + always-auto-confirm. Karen could move sliders all day; reconcile didn&rsquo;t care.</strong> The v1.34.7 changelog explicitly said &lsquo;SURFACE first, enforcement next so we don&rsquo;t silently change behavior on existing spas mid-ship&rsquo; — this is the enforcement ship. <strong>What changed</strong>: <code>reconcileRecoveryEventsForUser</code> (the cron-driven reconcile fn that scans unverified recovery events + tries to match each to a patient_transaction in a time window) now loads AttributionSettings from the tenant&rsquo;s knowledge_nodes row at the start of every pass and enforces three of them: (1) <code>enabled</code> &mdash; if false, the whole reconcile bails with zeroes (no QBO matching happens until Karen flips it back on); (2) <code>windowHours</code> &mdash; replaces the hardcoded 14 days. Default is 72h (3 days) per the v1.34.7 schema; spas can extend up to 720h (30 days); (3) <code>autoConfirmThresholdUsd</code> &mdash; threshold gate. Below threshold: auto-confirm (current behavior, stamps verified_at + amount + source=&lsquo;qbo&rsquo;); AT or above threshold: write the proposed amount + matched_transaction_id but leave verified_at NULL so Karen reviews on the Recovery surface. Threshold of 0 = always auto-confirm (the pre-v1.34.9.5 behavior). <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T enforce</strong>: <code>agentWeights</code> tie-break (Rescue 1.0 / Preshow 0.5 / Post-recovery 0.8) &mdash; deferred. Tie-break only matters when MULTIPLE agents could claim the same appointment, but recordRecoveryEvent is idempotent on appointment_id (first-writer-wins, second writer no-ops). Wiring weights properly requires multi-agent eligibility logic that doesn&rsquo;t exist yet (would need a recovery_event_candidates table or similar). Karen can tune the weight values in the UI but they&rsquo;re cosmetic until that substrate ships. <strong>Return shape extended</strong>: reconcileRecoveryEventsForUser now returns <code>{ matched, scanned, queuedForReview }</code> &mdash; the new third field counts at/above-threshold matches that got proposed data but stayed unverified. Additive change; existing callers&rsquo; destructures of matched + scanned keep working. <strong>Cron sweep</strong> (<code>api.cron.emma-reconcile.ts</code>) propagates the new counter into its summary JSON as <code>queued_for_review</code> so admin observability includes it. <strong>New export</strong>: <code>loadAttributionSettings</code> from refill-attribution-agent.functions.ts (was the private <code>loadSettings</code>) so dispatch can call the same default-fallback loader the UI uses &mdash; single-sourced. <strong>What this means for Karen</strong>: she can now actually tune the engine. Spas with low-volume / high-trust environments leave threshold at 0 and the engine auto-confirms everything (existing behavior). Spas with high-volume / cautious operators set threshold to e.g. $500 and only big-ticket matches get auto-confirmed; everything else queues for manual review on /app/refill/recovery. Pausing master toggle = no reconcile until she turns it back on (useful during EOM accounting close-outs). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/server/refill-attribution-agent.functions.ts</code> (loadSettings → exported as loadAttributionSettings wrapper), <code>src/server/emma-attribution.functions.ts</code> (import loadAttributionSettings + load at reconcile start + bail-if-disabled + windowMs from settings.windowHours + threshold-gated auto-confirm vs queue-for-review + queuedForReview counter), <code>src/routes/api.cron.emma-reconcile.ts</code> (propagate queuedForReview into summary JSON), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No new dependencies; no schema change.",
