      "<strong>v1.34.8 &mdash; iMessage MCP delivery integration. The closing ship that turns Recognition Allocation suggestions into actual blue-bubble sends through Karen&rsquo;s Apple ID. The v1.34 arc is now complete.</strong> Pre-ship: v1.34.5 generated allocation suggestions Karen could Confirm or Dismiss, but Confirm was a local note — no actual outreach. Post-ship: Karen confirms N suggestions, taps &lsquo;Dispatch N via iMessage&rsquo;, Refill composes per-cohort messages with variable substitution, sends a single batch email to the spa&rsquo;s rescue_proxy_email, Karen pastes the email body into Claude Desktop with the iMessage MCP installed, MCP calls <code>draft_imessage(recipient_phone, body)</code> per row, one Messages.app conversation per draft, Karen reviews + taps Send. The blue bubble lands as <em>from Karen</em>, not from a platform shortcode &mdash; the architectural primitive incumbents structurally can&rsquo;t match. <strong>Per-cohort message templates</strong>: <code>AllocationSettings.templates</code> extended with three Karen-voice defaults &mdash; Loyal Vintage (relationship-celebrating, references tenure), Top-Decile Current (impact-celebrating, references the spa name), At-Risk (warm check-in, no pressure). Editable from <code>/app/refill/agents/recognition</code> &lsquo;iMessage templates per cohort&rsquo; section. Variables supported: <code>{{firstName}}</code>, <code>{{brand}}</code>, <code>{{units}}</code>, <code>{{spaName}}</code>, <code>{{manufacturer}}</code>. <strong>New server fn</strong> <code>dispatchAllocationBatch(suggestionIds: uuid[])</code>: loads each confirmed suggestion + the patient&rsquo;s phone from knowledge_nodes, skips patients without phones (returned in result.skipped), loads spa proxy email + spa name, composes per-row drafts using the cohort&rsquo;s template, sends a single batch email via Resend (same infrastructure as v379 waitlist invites &mdash; reuses fromEmail + html template style + auto-send header), flips each dispatched suggestion&rsquo;s status from &lsquo;confirmed&rsquo; → &lsquo;dispatched&rsquo;. Suggestion status union extended with &lsquo;dispatched&rsquo;. Skip reason &lsquo;no rescue_proxy_email set&rsquo; surfaces if the spa hasn&rsquo;t configured one. <strong>UI</strong>: Recognition Agent header gains a conditional &lsquo;Dispatch N via iMessage&rsquo; button (shows count of confirmed-not-yet-dispatched). Templates editor section above the allocation queue with one textarea per cohort + variable-hint footer + Save button. Suggestion row gains a Dispatched status pill (filled emerald, distinct from the Confirmed outline). The full lifecycle is now visible in one place: Pending → Confirmed → Dispatched. <strong>Architecture anchor</strong> per <code>project_imessage_mcp_killer_arch</code>: Karen-Mac MCP setup happened 2026-05-31 &mdash; no client work needed on her side. The Refill → Resend email → Claude Desktop iMessage MCP pipeline matches the v379 waitlist invite pattern proven on real Acuity data 2026-06-01. v1.34.8 extends that pipeline to Recognition. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T ship</strong>: webhook callback from Karen-Mac to mark which drafts were actually sent vs deleted (status flips to &lsquo;dispatched&rsquo; on email-send, not on iMessage-send &mdash; the latter would need a Karen-Mac → Refill callback that&rsquo;s deferred); per-patient template override (uses cohort template uniformly); A/B template variants per cohort with performance tracking; auto-resend if a draft was deleted unsent; opt-out tracking back to the patient knowledge_node (currently the Refill opt-out flow stays separate); per-brand template variants. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/server/refill-recognition-allocation.functions.ts</code> (AllocationSettings.templates field + dispatchAllocationBatch fn + suggestion status &lsquo;dispatched&rsquo;), <code>src/routes/app.refill.agents.recognition.tsx</code> (Send/MessageSquareText icon imports + draftTpls state + saveTemplates + dispatchConfirmed handlers + templates editor section + Dispatch CTA in PageHeader actions + Dispatched status pill), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; reuses existing knowledge_nodes pattern for settings + reuses Resend infrastructure. <strong>Strategic anchor</strong>: per [[project-recognition-allocation-engine-spec]] and [[project-imessage-mcp-killer-arch]] this closes the Recognition loop. Allergan-spend → rebate units → Recognition Agent allocates to right cohort → Karen-voice iMessage drafts → blue-bubble send → patient feels recognized → continues buying Allergan. The compounding flywheel is now end-to-end on real infrastructure.",
