      "<strong>v1.34.4 &mdash; Per-treatment-type cadence overrides on the Preshow Agent. The last leg of Preshow Agent surface completeness.</strong> Pre-ship: every patient in a profile got the same cadence regardless of treatment type &mdash; Botox (3-month repeat cycle, low show-rate cost) and laser (1-year repeat cycle, high anesthesia prep cost) both got 48/24/3h reminders. Post-ship: Karen can override cadence per treatment-type per profile &mdash; e.g., set <code>botox → 72, 24, 12</code> while everything else uses the profile&rsquo;s spa-wide cadence. The JSONB column <code>cadence_by_treatment_type</code> was reserved on <code>emma_preshow_profiles</code> in the v1.34.3 migration; v1.34.4 wires the UI + dispatch logic on top of it without any schema change. <strong>UI</strong> (<code>/app/refill/agents/preshow</code>): ProfileCard gains a new collapsible expander &lsquo;Per-treatment-type cadence overrides&rsquo; between Tone+Channel and Per-touchpoint messages, with Layers icon. Inline list shows existing overrides as treatment-type pill + array of hour chips + Remove button per row. &lsquo;Add override&rsquo; form: treatment-type text input (case-insensitive, lowercased on save) + comma/space-delimited hours csv input + Add button. Validation: hours 0-8760, dedupe, sort descending. Empty state copy: &lsquo;No overrides yet. Treatments not listed here use the spa-wide cadence above.&rsquo; Help copy: &lsquo;Treatment types match against appointment.treatment_type case-insensitive. Example: botox → 72, 24, 12 overrides the spa-wide cadence for any Botox appointment.&rsquo; <strong>Server fn</strong>: <code>updatePreshowProfile</code> input schema gains optional <code>cadenceByTreatmentType: Record&lt;string, number[]&gt;</code> field. Handler filters out empty arrays before writing (lets the UI clear a single override by sending an empty array). <strong>Dispatch rewire</strong> (<code>src/server/emma-preshow.functions.ts</code>): the resolved profile&rsquo;s SELECT now includes <code>cadence_hours</code> + <code>cadence_by_treatment_type</code> (was just <code>id, tone, channel</code>). After profile resolution but before tone/channel resolution: if <code>profile.cadence_by_treatment_type[apt.treatment_type.toLowerCase().trim()]</code> exists and is non-empty, the dispatch checks if <code>offsetHours</code> is in that array. If not, returns a new skip reason <code>outside_treatment_cadence</code> (added to <code>PreShowSkipReason</code> union) with message &lsquo;Treatment-type override for &lsquo;X&rsquo; doesn&rsquo;t include T-Nh.&rsquo; <strong>Cron rewire</strong> (<code>src/routes/api.cron.emma-preshow-sweep.ts</code>): the per-spa offset-union now includes BOTH each profile&rsquo;s spa-wide <code>cadence_hours</code> AND every value array in each profile&rsquo;s <code>cadence_by_treatment_type</code>. This is the right safety: the sweep catches every appointment that might need a reminder at this offset; <code>dispatchPreShowReminder</code> enforces per-treatment scoping. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T ship</strong>: autocomplete of existing treatment-types from <code>emma_appointments.treatment_type</code> distinct values (Karen types free-text for now); per-treatment-type tone or channel override (uniform within profile); per-treatment-type custom message template (uses the profile&rsquo;s message templates uniformly &mdash; future ship could let overrides have their own templates); treatment-type alias mapping (e.g., &lsquo;tox&rsquo; &harr; &lsquo;botox&rsquo;); per-treatment-type performance counters (the 7-day metrics attribute to profile-level only). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/server/refill-preshow-agent.functions.ts</code> (updateProfileInput zod schema + handler), <code>src/server/emma-preshow.functions.ts</code> (PreShowSkipReason union + profileRow shape + per-treatment override check), <code>src/routes/api.cron.emma-preshow-sweep.ts</code> (union over per-treatment override hours too), <code>src/routes/app.refill.agents.preshow.tsx</code> (Layers icon import + state + handlers + collapsible expander + override list + add form), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no nav change; no new deps. <strong>Strategic anchor</strong>: closes Preshow Agent feature surface completeness &mdash; profile + cadence + per-touchpoint messages + tone + channel + patient routing (v1.34.3.1) + per-treatment override (v1.34.4). v1.34.5 unlocks the Recognition Allocation 4th agent on top of this proven pattern.",
