      "<strong>v1.34.3.1 &mdash; Patient routing for the Preshow Agent. The bridge ship that turns v1.34.3&rsquo;s named-profiles substrate into a real Chronic-vs-Default outcome on the spa floor.</strong> Pre-ship: Karen could create a Chronic profile with a 5d/3d/48h/24h/12h cadence at <code>/app/refill/agents/preshow</code>, but every patient still routed to the spa-wide Default profile because no UI existed to assign a patient to a non-default profile. Profiles were a substrate without an outcome. Post-ship: Karen routes patients to ANY profile from two surfaces &mdash; one chip click on the patient detail page (per-patient), one bulk-tag pass on the patient list (per-cohort, up to 2000 at a time). Dispatch reads the per-patient routing on every reminder. <strong>Per-patient detail page picker</strong> (<code>/app/refill/patients/$patientId</code>): SoftTagsCard gains a new &lsquo;Preshow profile&rsquo; row at the top of the seeded six. Same EnumTagRow UX as Income tier / Negotiator / etc. &mdash; tap to expand, chip per profile (Default chip labeled &lsquo;Default &middot; default&rsquo;), Reason field (optional), Save / Clear. Renders only when at least one profile exists (defense-in-depth; v1.34.3 backfill guarantees every spa has one). Value pill shows the live profile name resolved from the loaded profiles list. Edge case: if the routed profile was deleted, dispatch silently falls back to the default profile so a stale routing never blocks a reminder. <strong>Per-cohort bulk picker</strong> (<code>/app/refill/patients</code>): BulkTagPickerModal gains a third section &lsquo;Preshow profile (Agents &middot; routes reminders)&rsquo; between Preset tags and Custom tags. One chip per tenant profile, mutually exclusive, with sub-text &lsquo;Override the spa-wide default for these patients only.&rsquo; Click apply &rarr; bulkApplyPatientSoftTag writes <code>softTags.preshowProfileId = { value: profileId, setByUserId, setAt, reason }</code> across all selected patient rows in one batched in-memory merge (50/batch up to 2000 patients). Toast resolves the profile UUID back to the profile name for the success message (&lsquo;Preshow profile: Chronic applied to 47 patients.&rsquo;). <strong>Type extension</strong>: <code>PatientSoftTags.preshowProfileId?: PatientSoftTagEntry&lt;string&gt; | null</code> &mdash; UUID of the routed profile, full provenance entry shape (setByUserId, setAt, reason) matching the seeded six tags. Stored on knowledge_nodes.attachments.softTags so it follows the existing tenant-scoped read pattern (no new table). <strong>Server fn updates</strong>: <code>setPatientSoftTag</code> discriminated union gains <code>{ key: &lsquo;preshowProfileId&rsquo;, value: z.string().uuid() }</code> branch; <code>clearPatientSoftTag</code> key enum gains &lsquo;preshowProfileId&rsquo;; <code>bulkApplyPatientSoftTag</code> preset.key enum gains &lsquo;preshowProfileId&rsquo; (the in-memory merge code was already generic so no handler change). <strong>Dispatch rewire</strong> (<code>src/server/emma-preshow.functions.ts</code>): the v1.34.3 default-profile lookup at section 3.5 now reads <code>patient.softTags.preshowProfileId?.value</code> first; if set, resolves THAT profile by id; if missing OR the routed profile was deleted, falls back to the is_default=true profile. patientAttachments cast extended to include softTags.preshowProfileId. Same downstream behavior for tone + channel + template lookup &mdash; just sourced from the routed profile instead of always the default. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T ship (queued)</strong>: per-treatment-type cadence overrides (v1.34.4; column reserved on profiles in v1.34.3 migration); auto-detect chronic-rescheduler patients from emma_appointment_status_events history (v1.34.3.x; Karen manually tags in v1.34.3.1); profile-drift visibility on /app/admin/agents (v1.34.3.x); Rescue + Attribution surfaces (v1.34.6 / v1.34.7 mirror Preshow); Recognition Allocation as 4th agent (v1.34.5 per the locked Recognition hybrid framing); email-channel template rendering (SMS-only stays in v1.34.3 / v1.34.3.1). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/lib/patient-csv.ts</code> (PatientSoftTags type gains preshowProfileId entry), <code>src/server/patient-ingest.functions.ts</code> (softTagWriteInput + softTagClearInput + bulkApplyInput zod schemas all gain preshowProfileId), <code>src/server/emma-preshow.functions.ts</code> (patientAttachments cast extended; dispatch section 3.5 resolves routed-profile-first with default-profile fallback), <code>src/routes/app.refill.patients.$patientId.tsx</code> (listPreshowProfiles loaded alongside getPatientById; SoftTagsCard takes preshowProfiles prop and renders new EnumTagRow at the top of the seeded six), <code>src/routes/app.refill.patients.index.tsx</code> (listPreshowProfiles loaded alongside list/overdue/waitlist/defs; BulkTagPickerModal takes preshowProfiles prop and renders new third section with one chip per profile; bulkApply tag type union widened to accept preshowProfileId key; apply formatter resolves profile name for toast), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no nav change; no new dependencies. <strong>Strategic anchor</strong>: per [[project-wishlist-thesis]] this is the &lsquo;7 lines from substrate to floor&rsquo; ship &mdash; v1.34.3 laid 3 new tables + 9 server fns + 1 full agent surface; v1.34.3.1 adds 7 small edits across 6 files and the substrate becomes a Chronic-vs-Default outcome on Karen&rsquo;s real 1,140-patient roster. Per [[feedback-verify-deploy-after-push]] this ship was deployed via explicit <code>npm run deploy</code> + bundle-hash verification.",
