      "<strong>v1.34.0.1 &mdash; Five UX fixes caught during Grasshopper&rsquo;s v1.34.0 dry-run walk-through. All small, all annoying, all surfaced inside ~30 minutes of real use.</strong> Per the meta-loop the Wishlist proves: every friction Karen hits in production becomes a banked hotfix in the next ship. This is the receipt. <strong>Fix 1 &mdash; Markdown rendering on Wishlist description</strong>: the v1.33.1 AI polish returns the buildable spec as markdown (<code>**What**: ...</code>, <code>- bullet</code>), but the admin inbox and Karen&rsquo;s My-requests panel both rendered literal asterisks. New <code>MarkdownLight</code> component handles <code>**bold**</code> + <code>- bullets</code> + paragraph breaks &mdash; minimal renderer, no react-markdown dependency. Wired into both the admin row description and Karen&rsquo;s My-requests expanded view. <strong>Fix 2 &mdash; Filter chips vs Move-status chips visually distinct</strong>: prior version had two sets of identical-looking pill chips with the same status labels (Submitted / Reviewing / Building / Shipped / Declined) in two different places on the admin inbox &mdash; one as &lsquo;narrow this view&rsquo; (filter), one as &lsquo;mutate this wish&rsquo; (move status). Grasshopper got fluky clicks because they looked the same. Now: filter chips keep the pill shape + add a Filter funnel icon next to the &lsquo;Filter&rsquo; label. Move-status chips become a single segmented control (rounded rectangle, dividers between options) + ArrowRight icon next to the &lsquo;Move status:&rsquo; label. Clear semantic + visual distinction. <strong>Fix 3 &mdash; Filter chip counts show TRUE DB totals</strong>: prior version computed counts from the loaded <code>requests</code> array, which only contained the currently-filtered subset &mdash; so &lsquo;Shipped 0&rsquo; was misleading when there were 2 shipped wishes hidden by the filter. Now always loads ALL wishes server-side and filters client-side (volume justifies it &mdash; ~100s per tenant max). Counts now reflect the real database totals regardless of which chips are active. <strong>Fix 4 &mdash; Default filter = &lsquo;Show all&rsquo; on landing</strong>: prior default was Submitted+Reviewing+Building active (hiding Shipped+Declined). Grasshopper landed on the admin inbox, didn&rsquo;t see his wishes, had to UN-click each active chip OR add the missing ones &mdash; non-obvious either way. Now: default state is empty filter = show everything. Tapping a chip ADDS a narrow-by filter. New &lsquo;Show all&rsquo; link appears when 1+ chips are active, instantly clears. Also adds a new &lsquo;N of M shown&rsquo; counter on the right of the chip strip so you always know how much is visible vs hidden. The empty state copy now splits: &lsquo;No requests yet&rsquo; (truly empty DB) vs &lsquo;No requests match the current filter &middot; Show all N&rsquo; (filtered-out). <strong>Fix 5 &mdash; Reply send double-click idempotency</strong>: prior version&rsquo;s Send button relied on the <code>busy</code> state to disable, but a fast second click could fire before React rendered the disabled state (Grasshopper hit it during the Galderma close-out &mdash; sent the same reply twice). Both <code>WishlistWidget.sendReply</code> and <code>AdminRequestRow.sendReply</code> now: (a) bail if <code>busy</code> is already true, (b) OPTIMISTICALLY clear the draft on click so the button instantly disables via the empty-body check, (c) restore the draft if the server call fails. Same-text duplicate replies prevented; user retry path preserved on real errors. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: server-side dedup (a network retry could theoretically still dupe if the request actually succeeded but the response was lost &mdash; rare; would need an idempotency-key column on wishlist_replies, deferred unless it bites). Markdown features beyond bold + bullets + paragraphs (no italics, no inline code, no links &mdash; the polish format doesn&rsquo;t use them). Bulk reply-to-all / template replies on admin side. SLA-timeline cleanup of fluky workflow noise from earlier sessions (timestamps are correct, just visually noisy). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/components/MarkdownLight.tsx</code> (NEW &mdash; ~80 lines, parses bold/bullets/paragraphs, no deps), <code>src/routes/app.admin.wishlist.tsx</code> (Filter+ArrowRight icon imports + MarkdownLight import + always-load-all in load fn + visibleRequests client-side filter useMemo + default empty filter + clearFilters helper + Filter label + Show all link + N of M counter + segmented Move status control + MarkdownLight on description + sendReply double-click guard), <code>src/components/WishlistWidget.tsx</code> (MarkdownLight import + render description via MarkdownLight in My-requests panel + sendReply double-click guard with optimistic clear + restore-on-error), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no nav change; no new dependencies.",
