      "<strong>v1.34.0 &mdash; Bulk soft-tag apply. Karen&rsquo;s first AI-polished Wishlist becomes a shipped feature, completing the customer-wish &rarr; production-ship loop in one session arc.</strong> The wish that landed via v1.33.1&rsquo;s AI-assist flow (&lsquo;add bulk-set so I can apply a soft tag to many patients at once&rsquo;) is now a real platform feature: checkbox each patient row, &lsquo;Select all visible&rsquo; in the table header, a floating bottom-bar action toolbar with count + Apply soft tag + Clear, and a picker modal that surfaces ALL tag taxonomies in one place &mdash; seeded six + tenant-wide custom defs from v1.31.5 &mdash; with chip selection, optional reason note, and one-click apply across the selection. <strong>What ships</strong>: (1) <code>bulkApplyPatientSoftTag</code> server fn in <code>patient-ingest.functions.ts</code>: accepts patientNodeIds[] + a discriminated-union tag spec (preset key+value OR custom definitionId+selected[]) + optional reason. Single read of all selected patient attachments &rarr; in-memory merge of softTags / customSelections &rarr; parallelized per-row updates in batches of 50 (handles Karen-Rejuv&rsquo;s 1140-patient max cleanly in ~23 batched round-trips). Idempotent: patients already carrying the same tag value are silent no-ops, counted as &lsquo;skipped&rsquo; in the result. Returns <code>{touched, skipped}</code> for accurate toast feedback. Threaded through <code>resolveEffectiveUserId</code> for admin viewAs honored. setByUserId/setAt provenance captured per merged tag like every other soft-tag write. (2) Patient list state extended in <code>app.refill.patients.index.tsx</code>: <code>selectedIds: Set&lt;string&gt;</code> selection state, <code>bulkPickerOpen</code> modal state, <code>customDefs</code> loaded once on mount alongside patient list. Selection helpers: <code>toggleSelected</code>, <code>clearSelection</code>, <code>toggleSelectAllVisible</code> (intersect-with-filtered semantics: select-all-visible adds the filtered subset to the selection without clobbering out-of-filter selections; same for clear-visible). <code>visibleIds</code> / <code>selectedVisibleCount</code> / <code>allVisibleSelected</code> / <code>someVisibleSelected</code> derived from the existing <code>filtered</code> useMemo so filter changes don&rsquo;t lose selection. (3) <code>PatientRow</code> extended with <code>selected</code> + <code>onToggleSelected</code> props. New checkbox column at position 0 (8px wide); clicks <code>stopPropagation</code> so they don&rsquo;t navigate via the row Link. Selected rows render with emerald-soft background tint. Table header gains a matching checkbox cell with indeterminate state via React ref. (4) Floating bottom-center action toolbar (fixed bottom-6 left-1/2, z-40) appears the moment 1+ patients are selected: shows count + emerald &lsquo;Apply soft tag&rsquo; button + Clear. Mirrors the Sonner toast position pattern. (5) <code>BulkTagPickerModal</code> component &mdash; fixed inset-0 z-50 backdrop, centered card. Body lists all preset tag groups (Income tier / Negotiator / Specials seeker / Personality / Shopper loyalty &mdash; Cultural notes skipped because free-text doesn&rsquo;t fit bulk-set semantics) with chip selectors that single-select per group, then tenant-wide custom tag defs below with multi-select chip toggle. Reason note input. Apply button shows total count and chains into <code>bulkApply</code> handler. (6) <code>bulkApply</code> handler: calls server fn, surfaces success toast with proper grammar (&lsquo;Snowbird applied to 43 patients&rsquo; vs &lsquo;Snowbird applied to 43 patients (5 already had it)&rsquo;), clears selection, closes modal. Error toast surfaces server-side messages without losing the user&rsquo;s selection. <strong>Strategic significance</strong>: this is the first end-to-end demonstration of the project_wishlist_thesis loop: customer (Grasshopper-as-Karen) submitted a feature wish via the in-product Wishlist (v1.33.0), AI-assisted it to a buildable spec (v1.33.1), Po built it in one continuous session push, customer can now mark it &lsquo;shipped&rsquo; in the admin inbox via the same Wishlist. The 48h SLA promise is now structurally provable: timestamp on the wish submission + timestamp on the changelog entry below = same evening. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T ship</strong>: bulk-REMOVE (only apply for v1.34.0 &mdash; remove/clear deferred to v1.34.0.x if requested). Server-side RPC for sub-second 1000-patient apply (current batched-Promise.all is fast enough at this volume; promote to RPC if a 5000+ patient tenant arrives). Bulk apply for cultural notes (free-text isn&rsquo;t a bulk-set semantic; per-patient still works). Audit log of who-bulk-applied-what-to-whom (per-tag provenance lives on each touched patient via setByUserId/setAt, but a centralized bulk-action log is a future tenant-ops ship). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/server/patient-ingest.functions.ts</code> (new bulkApplyPatientSoftTag server fn with discriminated-union zod validator + idempotent merge logic + batched parallel writes with error aggregation), <code>src/routes/app.refill.patients.index.tsx</code> (selection state + visibleIds derivations + toggleSelected/clearSelection/toggleSelectAllVisible helpers + bulkApply handler + customDefs load alongside patient list + Check/Tag/X icon imports + sonner toast import + CustomTagDefinition type import + checkbox column header + checkbox column cell on PatientRow with stopPropagation + emerald-tinted selected row state + floating bottom action toolbar + BulkTagPickerModal sub-component with PRESET_TAGS catalog + BulkPickerSelection discriminated union + custom-def chip multi-select), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no nav change.",
