      "<strong>v1.33.1 &mdash; AI-assist in the Wishlist: title &rarr; draft &rarr; polish &rarr; dev-cost preview. The meta-loop&rsquo;s first fulfillment.</strong> Grasshopper&rsquo;s second submitted wish (after the Galderma-rebate ask that was actually the Recognition Allocation Engine) was for AI-assist on the Wishlist itself: type a title, get a draft description in your voice; edit, get a polished buildable spec; see a one-line dev-cost preview before submitting. v1.33.1 ships exactly that, completing the meta-loop the v1.33.0 ship started: customer wishes for a feature in the Wishlist, customer gets the feature, all inside the 48h SLA window the platform promises. <strong>What ships</strong>: (1) Three new server fns in <code>src/server/wishlist.functions.ts</code>: <code>aiDraftWishlistDescription</code> (Claude Sonnet 4.6, no thinking, low effort &mdash; takes a title, returns 3-5 sentences in Karen&rsquo;s voice with concrete front-desk examples and no developer jargon), <code>aiPolishWishlistDescription</code> (Sonnet 4.6, adaptive thinking, medium effort, structured-output JSON schema enforced via Anthropic&rsquo;s <code>output_config.format</code> &mdash; returns WHAT / WHY / WHERE / acceptance criteria; Zod-validated server-side after parse), and <code>aiEstimateWishlistBuild</code> (Sonnet 4.6, no thinking, low effort, max_tokens 128 &mdash; returns a one-line cost preview like &lsquo;~45 min build &middot; scoped for v1.34.0&rsquo;). (2) All three fns gated through <code>resolveEffectiveUserId</code> + <code>getTenantIdForUser</code> so AI cost only fires for authenticated spa-owners with a tenant. (3) Typed Anthropic error translation via <code>translateAnthropicError</code> helper: <code>RateLimitError</code> &rarr; &lsquo;try again in 30s&rsquo;, <code>AuthenticationError</code> &rarr; &lsquo;ANTHROPIC_API_KEY missing&rsquo;, generic <code>APIError</code> &rarr; surfaced message. (4) <strong>Widget UX</strong> additions in <code>src/components/WishlistWidget.tsx</code>: <em>Title &rarr; draft</em> &mdash; after title hits 5+ chars AND description is empty, two affordances appear under the title input: emerald-tinted &lsquo;&#10024; AI-assist description&rsquo; button + plain &lsquo;Skip &mdash; I&rsquo;ll write my own&rsquo; link (focuses textarea on click). <em>Description &rarr; polish</em> &mdash; after description hits 20+ chars AND no polish is pending, &lsquo;&#10024; Polish into buildable spec&rsquo; button appears under the textarea. <em>Polish compare</em> &mdash; the new <code>PolishComparePanel</code> renders side-by-side: &lsquo;Your words&rsquo; (her original, preserved) vs &lsquo;Polished spec&rsquo; (WHAT/WHY/WHERE/AC) with &lsquo;Use polish&rsquo; / &lsquo;Keep mine&rsquo; buttons. Accepting writes a markdown-formatted version of the spec into the description field; rejecting clears polish + estimate state. <em>Po&rsquo;s reading</em> &mdash; while estimate is computing OR after it lands, an emerald summary card appears above Submit: &lsquo;Po&rsquo;s reading &middot; ~30 min build &middot; scoped for v1.34.0&rsquo;. Karen builds dev-cost intuition before submitting. (5) Estimate generation chains off polish acceptance &mdash; non-blocking; if estimate fails, polish is still usable (toast notes the failure but doesn&rsquo;t roll back the polish). (6) Submit clears polish + estimate state alongside the draft. <strong>Why Sonnet 4.6 not Opus 4.7</strong>: interactive UX (Karen waiting in modal), Sonnet&rsquo;s adaptive thinking + medium effort is the sweet spot for spec-writing quality + sub-3s response. Skill default would be Opus 4.7; explicitly downshifted to Sonnet 4.6 for this interactive surface. <strong>Why not Haiku 4.5</strong>: spec polish needs reasoning; Haiku would flatten Karen&rsquo;s voice in the draft pass too. <strong>Why no prompt caching in v1.33.1</strong>: system prompts at ~600-900 tokens are below the 2048-token minimum cacheable prefix on Sonnet 4.6 (4096 on Haiku 4.5). At spa-owner volume (~1-10 wishes/day), the cost difference is negligible. Will revisit if usage justifies. <strong>Zod version note</strong>: project is on Zod v3; <code>@anthropic-ai/sdk/helpers/zod</code>&rsquo;s <code>zodOutputFormat</code> requires Zod v4. Worked around by passing the JSON schema directly to <code>output_config.format</code> as <code>{type: &quot;json_schema&quot;, schema: POLISHED_SPEC_JSON_SCHEMA}</code> (hand-written, mirrors <code>PolishedSpecSchema</code>), then validating the response at runtime via <code>PolishedSpecSchema.parse(JSON.parse(text))</code>. Same safety either way; no SDK version coupling. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: streaming the draft / polish responses (short outputs, streaming complexity not worth it). Per-tenant cost caps (every authenticated spa-owner can call AI fns freely &mdash; rate limits will surface naturally). Prompt caching (deferred). Multi-language drafts (English-only system prompt). Visible token / cost reporting per submission. Auto-trigger on debounce (Karen must tap the button &mdash; no surprise AI fires). <strong>Setup required</strong>: <code>npm install @anthropic-ai/sdk</code> + <code>npx wrangler secret put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code> for the worker. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>package.json</code> + <code>package-lock.json</code> (anthropic SDK + deps), <code>src/server/wishlist.functions.ts</code> (3 new server fns + JSON schema constant + Anthropic client helper + error translator + PolishedSpecSchema + 3 zod input validators), <code>src/components/WishlistWidget.tsx</code> (5 new state hooks for AI flow + 3 handler fns + acceptPolish/rejectPolish + draft input AI-assist buttons + polish compare panel + Po&rsquo;s reading preview card + Sparkles icon import), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no nav change.",
