      "<strong>v1.33.0 &mdash; Wishlist: the 48h-customization-SLA in-product surface lands. The MOAT ships.</strong> Per project_wishlist_thesis (banked 2026-06-01): customer-requested feature build IS the competitive moat. Po-compression means Refill can ship per-tenant customizations in 48h or less &mdash; structurally impossible for every med-spa-software incumbent (Vagaro, Mindbody, Square, Zenoti, Boulevard) because their build pipelines are weeks-to-quarters, not hours. v1.33.0 is the in-product affordance that turns the thesis from a sales line into an operational loop: spa-owner submits request, Grasshopper triages, Po ships, status updates land in the spa-owner&rsquo;s feed. The whole thing happens inside the app. <strong>The meta-moment that drove this ship</strong>: Grasshopper wished for a Wishlist feature mid-session, watched Po build it inline, and saw it deploy live within minutes. That&rsquo;s the demo Karen will see when she submits her first request. <strong>What ships</strong>: (1) New <code>wishlist_requests</code> table with full schema: user_id (spa-owner) + tenant_id (spa account) FKs, title + description + auto-captured area context + priority enum (low / normal / high / urgent) + status enum (submitted / reviewing / in_progress / shipped / declined), JSONB messages array for inline reply thread, admin_notes + shipped_in_version fields, per-status timestamps for SLA metrics (reviewing_at, in_progress_at, shipped_at, declined_at) populated by trigger on status change. 3 indexes for hot paths. (2) RLS: spa-owners read+insert own; admins (per user_roles) read+update all; service-role bypass for daemons. (3) Five new server fns in <code>src/server/wishlist.functions.ts</code>: <code>submitWishlistRequest</code> (tenant), <code>listMyWishlistRequests</code> (tenant), <code>addReplyToWishlistRequest</code> (either side appends to thread), <code>listAllWishlistRequests</code> (admin cross-tenant with denormalized tenant name + submitter email), <code>updateWishlistRequestStatus</code> (admin, with shipped_in_version + admin_notes). All threaded through <code>resolveEffectiveUserId</code> + <code>requireAdmin</code> per existing patterns. (4) New <code>WishlistWidget</code> floating component &mdash; bottom-right lightbulb-icon launcher on every <code>/app/refill/*</code> page (hidden on <code>/app/admin/*</code>). Modal with two tabs: <strong>New request</strong> (title + description + priority chip selector + auto-captured route as &ldquo;from&rdquo; chip + Submit, with success toast &ldquo;submitted &mdash; we&rsquo;ll respond in 48 hours or less&rdquo;) and <strong>My requests</strong> (her status feed with expandable rows showing description + admin notes + conversation thread + reply textarea). Mounted in RefillShellChrome so it appears on every authenticated spa-owner surface. (5) New <code>/app/admin/wishlist</code> admin inbox &mdash; cross-tenant request list with status filter chips (count per status), expandable rows showing full description, status workflow chip-buttons (submitted &rarr; reviewing &rarr; in_progress &rarr; shipped / declined), shipped_in_version + admin_notes inline editor, SLA timeline summary (submitted Xd ago &middot; reviewing Yh ago &middot; shipped Zm ago), conversation thread with admin replies styled distinctly, reply textarea + Send. Tenant name + submitter email denormalized into each row for triage clarity. (6) <code>ADMIN_SURFACES</code> array appended with the wishlist surface so it&rsquo;s discoverable from <code>/app/admin</code>. <strong>Migration storage decision</strong>: dedicated <code>wishlist_requests</code> table (not JSONB inside knowledge_nodes) because the admin inbox needs cross-tenant queries + status indexing + per-tenant filtering &mdash; all things a proper table indexes cleanly and JSONB doesn&rsquo;t. <strong>Reply thread storage</strong>: JSONB <code>messages[]</code> column for v1.33.0 simplicity; upgrade to separate table only if reply volume justifies. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T ship</strong>: Resend email notifications on status change (Resend is wired in <code>src/server/resend-gateway.ts</code> but the digest cadence + template needs its own v1.33.1 ship). Per-tenant config of which staff can submit (every authenticated user with a tenant membership can submit today). Public roadmap surface (intentionally not shipping &mdash; risks promising features Refill can&rsquo;t keep, breaks the 48h-or-decline promise). Auto-link &ldquo;shipped in vX.Y.Z&rdquo; to the actual git commit (manual field for now). Tenant-side notification when admin replies (status feed shows it on next open; bell-icon pulse is a v1.33.1 candidate). <strong>What this UNBLOCKS strategically</strong>: every customer conversation now has a built-in &ldquo;here&rsquo;s where you submit feature ideas&rdquo; close. Every Wishlist that ships becomes a marketing asset (the original request + the v-pill it shipped under is a verifiable receipt for the next prospect). The 48h SLA is now structurally measurable (per-status timestamps surface as cohort metrics later). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>supabase/migrations/20260602002954_v1_33_0_wishlist.sql</code> (NEW migration &mdash; spa-owner pastes into Supabase dashboard), <code>src/server/wishlist.functions.ts</code> (NEW &mdash; 5 server fns + types + hydrate helper + requireAdmin/getTenantIdForUser local copies matching the canonical_brands pattern), <code>src/components/WishlistWidget.tsx</code> (NEW &mdash; floating widget + modal with Submit + My requests tabs + reply thread), <code>src/routes/app.admin.wishlist.tsx</code> (NEW &mdash; admin inbox with status workflow + reply thread + SLA timeline + version stamp), <code>src/components/refill/RefillShellChrome.tsx</code> (mounts WishlistWidget), <code>src/routes/app.admin.index.tsx</code> (ADMIN_SURFACES append + Lightbulb icon import), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). Note: types.ts has not yet been regenerated for the new <code>wishlist_requests</code> table, so the server fns use <code>as never</code> casts at the supabase boundary &mdash; runtime is correct against the live schema once the migration paste lands.",
