      "<strong>v1.32.0 &mdash; Life-Event Log: substrate primitive #3 of the Profitability Engine (&sect;3.3) lands.</strong> Per spec &sect;3.3: timestamped events Karen captures (job loss, engagement, vacation, divorce, milestone-birthday, etc.) that modulate the static soft-tag profile for a TTL window. Sarah lost her job 2026-04-15 &rarr; ATP -30% for 180 days &rarr; the engine knows to discount-calibrate rather than upsell during that window, then auto-decays back to baseline. Sister primitive to Soft-Tags (v1.31): same Karen-set / never-inferred posture, same JSONB preservation through QB re-rolls. <strong>What ships</strong>: (1) <code>PatientLifeEvent</code> type with id + eventType + customLabel + eventDate + wtpModifier (-100..+100) + atpModifier (-100..+100) + ttlDays (or null = never decays) + reason + setByUserId + setAt provenance. 13 seeded event types: job_loss / promotion / engagement / marriage / divorce / new_baby / milestone_birthday / retirement / vacation / health_event / relocation / graduation / bereavement + custom. (2) <code>LIFE_EVENT_DEFAULTS</code> map per seeded type with industry-norm WTP / ATP / TTL: e.g., job_loss = WTP 0 / ATP -30% / 180d, engagement = WTP +25% / ATP 0 / 365d, milestone_birthday = WTP +30% / ATP 0 / 90d. Karen can override any default per event. (3) <code>isLifeEventActive</code> + <code>computeActiveModifiers</code> helpers: auto-decay is computed at READ time (not stored stale); aggregate WTP / ATP from all active events stack-sum-clamped to [-100, +100]. (4) Three new server fns: <code>addPatientLifeEvent</code> / <code>updatePatientLifeEvent</code> / <code>deletePatientLifeEvent</code>, all threaded through <code>resolveEffectiveUserId</code> for admin viewAs. (5) Life events stored on <code>knowledge_nodes.attachments.lifeEvents</code> with same preservation pattern as softTags &mdash; <code>extractContactSummary</code> + <code>rollupPatientSummary</code> merge block both extended. (6) <strong>New Life events card</strong> on patient detail, slotted between Soft tags and Purchase patterns. Active-modifier summary pill at top (&ldquo;3 active events &middot; WTP +15% &middot; ATP -30% &middot; next decay in 47d&rdquo;) when any event is active. Timeline list with active events first (most-recent), archived (auto-decayed) collapsible below. Each row shows: event label + date + WTP/ATP modifiers + TTL window + reason note. Inline edit (chip selector for event type, date picker, TTL input, dual range-slider for WTP/ATP modifiers, reason input). &ldquo;+ Add a life event&rdquo; affordance at the bottom of the active section. (7) Selecting a seeded event type auto-fills WTP / ATP / TTL with the industry-norm defaults; Karen can fine-tune via the sliders. Custom event types prompt for a free-form label. <strong>Why this matters strategically</strong>: this is the LIVE-DATA layer of the Profitability Engine. Soft-Tags + Catalog + Purchase Patterns are the static foundation; Life-Events tell the engine when a patient&rsquo;s real-world situation shifts so the static profile gets modulated. Without this, the engine treats every patient as if their economic / emotional state is frozen in time. With this, &ldquo;Sarah went through a divorce 4 months ago&rdquo; means engines know NOT to push high-margin Botox upsells this quarter; &ldquo;Karen mentioned her own engagement&rdquo; means the milestone-birthday engine knows to ramp recognition during the wedding-prep window. <strong>Profitability Engine scoring factor #17</strong> (Active life-event modifiers) now has a substrate. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: ML-inferred life events (we will NEVER do this &mdash; only Karen captures these from her direct conversations with patients). Cross-patient event templates (e.g., &lsquo;everyone in the area got hit by the layoffs&rsquo;). Reminder workflows (&lsquo;flag patients with active job_loss for re-engagement in 90d&rsquo; &mdash; v1.32.x candidate). Event-driven push notifications to Karen-Mac. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/lib/patient-csv.ts</code> (PatientLifeEvent + PatientLifeEventType + ActiveLifeEventModifier types + isLifeEventActive + computeActiveModifiers + LIFE_EVENT_DEFAULTS + lifeEvents field on PatientContactSummary + rollupPatientSummary merge), <code>src/server/patient-ingest.functions.ts</code> (PatientLifeEvent imports + PatientListRow extended with lifeEvents + hydratePatientListRow maps it through + extractContactSummary preserves lifeEvents + 3 new server fns sharing the mutateLifeEvents helper), <code>src/routes/app.refill.patients.$patientId.tsx</code> (LifeEventsCard + LifeEventRow + LifeEventForm + LIFE_EVENT_ORDER + eventLabel + LifeEventDraft + emptyLifeEventDraft + eventToDraft + applySeededDefaults flow + Heart and Clock icon imports + wired into detail page JSX with optimistic state mirror), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no nav change.",
