    date: "June 2026",
    items: [
      "<strong>v1.31.3 &mdash; TYPICAL cadence baseline added alongside PERSONAL: rewards programs + FDA windows now have a substrate.</strong> Per Grasshopper&rsquo;s mid-session callout: her personal cadence is great for &ldquo;is she slowing down?&rdquo;, but reward programs (Alle / Aspire / Merz Rewards) and FDA-label retreatment windows key off the TYPICAL / industry-standard cadence, not her personal pattern. Karen needs to see BOTH at a glance: she might be on-personal-cadence at 110 days for Botox (her own norm), but she&rsquo;s now past the 90-day TYPICAL window which means she&rsquo;s eligible for an Alle-rewards-mapped touchup nudge. v1.31.2 only tracked personal; v1.31.3 adds typical as a parallel signal across every dimension. <strong>What ships</strong>: (1) <code>CadenceWindow</code> in <code>patient-cadence.ts</code> gains <code>expectedDays</code> field; <code>KIND_CADENCE</code> defaults updated to Grasshopper&rsquo;s industry norms: toxin 90d expected (was implicitly 4mo soft), filler 270d expected (median of 6mo-2yr range), biostim 540d expected. Soft / lapsed windows unchanged. (2) <code>CadenceMetrics</code> in <code>patient-csv.ts</code> gains two new fields: <code>typicalExpectedDays</code> (typical retreatment interval for this dimension, null when not derivable) and <code>typicalStatus</code> (&lsquo;on-cadence&rsquo; / &lsquo;overdue&rsquo; / &lsquo;lapsed&rsquo; / &lsquo;unknown&rsquo; relative to the typical baseline). Existing <code>status</code> field continues to track personal-norm status (her own cadence). Both computed on every rollup. (3) <code>computeCadenceFromDates</code> now takes <code>typicalExpectedDays</code> + <code>typicalLapsedDays</code> as optional inputs; for daysSinceLastVisit ≤ expectedDays → on-cadence (eligible for rewards); past expected but ≤ lapsed → overdue; past lapsed → lapsed. (4) <code>computePurchasePatterns</code> resolves typical per dimension: byKind reads <code>KIND_CADENCE[kind]</code> directly; byManufacturer + byProduct derive typical from the DOMINANT kind of transactions for that group (e.g., a manufacturer whose transactions are mostly toxin gets the 90d typical; a product whose transactions are mostly filler gets the 270d typical). This means even brand-level / product-level cadence has a reward-program-relevant typical baseline. (5) <strong>UI flip</strong>: status pill on each Purchase patterns row now shows TYPICAL status (the action-relevant signal &mdash; &ldquo;On typical&rdquo; / &ldquo;Overdue (typical)&rdquo; / &ldquo;Lapsed (typical)&rdquo;). Personal status surfaces as a small secondary tag below the pill (&ldquo;personal: on/overdue/lapsed&rdquo;). Trend chip continues to track personal trajectory. New row-body line: <em>&ldquo;typical retreat 90d · 23d until eligible&rdquo;</em> (when on-cadence) or <em>&ldquo;typical retreat 90d · 12d past typical&rdquo;</em> (when overdue / lapsed). Karen sees in one scan: typical-vs-personal-vs-trend. (6) When the typical baseline is unknown (kind not in KIND_CADENCE), the row falls back to showing personal status as the primary pill, same as v1.31.2 behavior. <strong>Why this matters strategically</strong>: this is the reward-program substrate. The Recognition Allocation Engine spec (&sect;5.x) keys off &ldquo;eligible per manufacturer reward rules&rdquo; &mdash; that rule check now reads <code>patient.purchasePatterns.byKind.toxin.typicalStatus === &quot;on-cadence&quot;</code> directly. Same for Alle qualifying retreatments, Aspire windows, future FDA-label-keyed reminders. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: per-product typical override (Voluma 18-24mo vs Restylane 6-9mo &mdash; both currently fall back to filler-kind&rsquo;s 270d typical; per-brand typical map is a v1.31.4 candidate once Karen tags more products). Reward-program-specific windows (Alle requires retreatment within 28-60 days of last to qualify for tier 2, etc. &mdash; v1.31.4+ ships reward-program-specific cadence overlays). Population-norm typical (today&rsquo;s typical comes from <code>KIND_CADENCE</code> defaults; pulling actual Rejuv-tenant population means at scale is a v1.32+ aggregation ship). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/lib/patient-cadence.ts</code> (expectedDays field on CadenceWindow + KIND_CADENCE values updated for toxin / filler / biostim), <code>src/lib/patient-csv.ts</code> (CadenceMetrics extended with typicalExpectedDays + typicalStatus + KIND_CADENCE import + computeCadenceFromDates signature expanded + computePurchasePatterns extended with byMfrKindCounts and byProductKindCounts trackers and dominantKind / typicalForKind helpers), <code>src/routes/app.refill.patients.$patientId.tsx</code> (PatternRowView flips primary pill to typicalStatus + adds personal secondary tag + adds typical retreat reference line + StatusPill takes &lsquo;kind&rsquo; prop with typical / personal labels + personalStatusLabel helper), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no nav change.",
    ],
