    version: "v1.31.2",
    date: "June 2026",
    items: [
      "<strong>v1.31.2 &mdash; Per-patient purchase patterns: THE differentiator lands.</strong> Per Grasshopper&rsquo;s strategic frame mid-session: tracking each patient&rsquo;s individual purchase cadence across every kind, manufacturer, and specific product IS our moat. The engines downstream (no-show fill, Recognition Allocation, combo upsell, manufacturer-promoted moments, anniversary touch, life-event response) all need this substrate to target the right offer at the right time against THIS patient&rsquo;s real habits &mdash; not population averages. Karen&rsquo;s brain holds this for ~200 patients; the engine holds it for 1,140 (and 11,400). <strong>What ships</strong>: (1) New <code>computePurchasePatterns</code> function in <code>patient-csv.ts</code>: groups a patient&rsquo;s transactions by kind, manufacturer, AND specific product name, then computes per-group cadence metrics. (2) <code>CadenceMetrics</code> per dimension entry: <code>visitCount</code>, <code>firstVisit</code>, <code>lastVisit</code>, <code>lifetimeAvgDays</code> (avg interval across entire history), <code>recentAvgDays</code> (last 730 days, falls back to lifetime when patient tenure &lt;2yr or fewer than 2 recent visits), <code>daysSinceLastVisit</code>, <code>status</code> (on-cadence / overdue / lapsed relative to her OWN norm with 1.2x / 1.5x buffer thresholds), and <code>trend</code> (accelerating / steady / slowing &mdash; recent vs lifetime ratio with 15% threshold to avoid noise). (3) <code>PatientPurchasePatterns</code> struct: <code>byKind</code> + <code>byManufacturer</code> + <code>byProduct</code> branches, each a map from dimension key to <code>CadenceMetrics</code>. Per-product is keyed by raw product name (no normalization) so distinct QB entries stay distinct until Karen consolidates them in catalog. (4) Computed during <code>rollupPatientSummary</code> and stored on <code>knowledge_nodes.attachments.purchasePatterns</code>. Recomputed fresh on every rollup &mdash; pure derivation, never editorial. (5) <code>recomputePatientPatterns</code> server fn for single-patient on-demand recompute without re-uploading the whole QB CSV. Reuses <code>refreshPatientSummary</code> internally; viewAs-honored. (6) New <strong>Purchase patterns</strong> card on <code>/app/refill/patients/$id</code>, slotted right after Soft tags. Three bands: <em>Clinical (per kind)</em> &mdash; tox/filler/biostim/device/service/retail/reward pinned in clinical priority order; <em>By manufacturer</em> &mdash; top 5 with &ldquo;Show all N&rdquo; expander, sorted by visit count; <em>By product</em> &mdash; top 8 with &ldquo;Show all N&rdquo; expander, sorted by visit count. Each row shows label + visit count + lifetime avg cadence + recent avg cadence (when different) + days since last + next-expected projection + status pill + trend chip. (7) Empty-state card with a one-tap &ldquo;Compute patterns from transactions&rdquo; affordance for legacy patient rows that pre-date v1.31.2. (8) Excludes payment / discount / note transaction kinds from cadence computation &mdash; those aren&rsquo;t purchase events. Includes reward redemptions (Alle / Aspire) since they represent visits. <strong>How this collapses the v1.31.3 plan</strong>: per-product cadence makes per-filler-brand cadence (Voluma 18-24mo vs Restylane 6-9mo) fall out automatically from her actual visit data &mdash; no hard-coded brand-cadence map needed. v1.31.3 task closed, folded into this ship. <strong>Strategic impact</strong>: every Profitability Engine scoring factor 1-11 (gross margin / mix breadth / cadence regularity / trend slope / years as patient / referral generator / provider portability / current visit value / combo visit-shape / combo-rebate eligibility) now has a per-patient substrate to read against. Plus factor #4 (cadence regularity) is now directly readable, and factor #5 (trend slope) too. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: per-category rollup (filler-as-category isn&rsquo;t in <code>ProductKind</code> &mdash; service categories live in the catalog, not transaction kinds; rollup-by-category is a small future ship that joins transactions through the catalog table). Population-norm benchmarking (each patient is measured against her own norm; comparing &ldquo;Sarah&rsquo;s tox cadence vs all spa tox patients&rdquo; is a tenant-level aggregation ship). Backfill across all existing patients in a tenant in one shot (admin button or pg job; today each patient recomputes individually via the card button or a QB re-upload triggers full rollup). Per-injector cadence (when one patient sees two providers; needs provider attribution on transactions). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/lib/patient-csv.ts</code> (CadenceMetrics + PatientPurchasePatterns types + computeCadenceFromDates + computePurchasePatterns + daysBetween + daysSinceToday helpers + CADENCE_EXCLUDED_KINDS + wired into rollupPatientSummary), <code>src/server/patient-ingest.functions.ts</code> (PatientPurchasePatterns import + extended PatientListRow with purchasePatterns + hydratePatientListRow maps it + new recomputePatientPatterns server fn), <code>src/routes/app.refill.patients.$patientId.tsx</code> (PurchasePatternsCard + PatternBand + PatternRowView + StatusPill + TrendChip + KIND_PRIORITY + kindDisplayLabel + 4 new lucide icons + wired into detail page JSX with optimistic state mirror via onPatientChange), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no nav change.",
    ],
