      "<strong>v1.31.0 &mdash; Patient Soft-Tags: Karen&rsquo;s editorial layer lands on the patient detail page.</strong> First primitive of the Profitability Engine substrate (spec &sect;3.2) after the Catalog primitive shipped end-to-end last sesh (v1.29 &rarr; v1.30.1). Soft-Tags are the editorial signals only Karen can know &mdash; income tier, negotiator stance, specials-seeker flag, personality read, shopper loyalty, cultural / private notes &mdash; that her 16 years at the front desk taught her to track. The engine never infers these; they are Karen-tap-set only. Every entry carries provenance (set-by user + timestamp) plus an optional reason note Karen leaves to remind future-her what tipped her off. <strong>What ships</strong>: (1) Six tags on each patient: <code>incomeTier</code> (high &middot; mid &middot; low &middot; unknown), <code>negotiator</code> (never &middot; occasional &middot; always), <code>specialsSeeker</code> (yes &middot; no), <code>personality</code> (easy &middot; neutral &middot; complainer), <code>shopperLoyalty</code> (loyal &middot; comparison &middot; unknown), <code>culturalNotes</code> (free text, owner-private). (2) New &lsquo;Soft tags&rsquo; card on the patient detail page, slotted between Lifetime and Brand-mix. Inline-edit pattern (click a row, pick a chip, optional reason note, save) &mdash; no modal. Provenance footer shows when set. Clear-tag affordance per row. (3) Two new server fns &mdash; <code>setPatientSoftTag</code> and <code>clearPatientSoftTag</code> &mdash; both threaded through <code>resolveEffectiveUserId</code>, so admin viewing-as a tenant owner writes under the tenant&rsquo;s <code>user_id</code> with the admin&rsquo;s <code>auth.uid</code> recorded as <code>setByUserId</code> for audit. (4) Owner-only visibility is automatic: every read scopes by <code>effectiveUserId</code>, so cross-tenant leakage is structurally impossible. <strong>Zero-migration ship</strong>: tags live on <code>knowledge_nodes.attachments.softTags</code> (a field on the PatientSummary JSONB blob, same pattern as the v385.2 VIP flag). Survives QB re-imports via the rollup-preservation path. <strong>Latent v385.2 bug also fixed</strong>: <code>extractContactSummary</code> was missing <code>vip</code> propagation, meaning Karen&rsquo;s VIP picks were silently wiped on every sales-CSV re-upload since v385.2. The same one-line touch that adds <code>softTags</code> preservation also adds <code>vip</code> preservation &mdash; VIP designations now actually survive re-rolls as v385.2 originally intended. <strong>What this unblocks</strong>: scoring primitives 12-16 of the Profitability Engine &sect;4 (income tier &middot; willingness-to-pay &middot; specials-seeker negative &middot; personality &middot; shopper loyalty) all read directly from this layer. Karen can start tagging her real Rejuv patients as she works through them; the next ship (v1.x.2 Life-Events) and v1.x.3 (17-factor scoring) compose on top. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: bulk-tagging UI (Karen tags one patient at a time today &mdash; bulk surface comes after the A-list dashboard learns the patterns). Per-role visibility config (the spec calls out staff-practitioner scope as &sect;13 open-question #4; default is owner-only, which is what this ships). Tag change history (only most-recent entry stored; older values overwritten &mdash; if Karen revisits in 3 months, the prior reason note is gone). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/lib/patient-csv.ts</code> (new types: PatientSoftTagEntry generic + PatientSoftTags struct + 4 enum unions + PatientSoftTagKey + extension to PatientContactSummary), <code>src/server/patient-ingest.functions.ts</code> (extended PatientListRow with softTags + hydratePatientListRow maps it through + extractContactSummary preserves vip and softTags through re-rolls + new setPatientSoftTag and clearPatientSoftTag server fns with discriminated-union zod validation), <code>src/routes/app.refill.patients.$patientId.tsx</code> (SoftTagsCard + TagRowShell + EnumTagRow + BoolTagRow + TextTagRow + ChipButton + wired into the detail page JSX with local state mirror for optimistic updates), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no nav change.",
