      "<strong>v1.30.0 &mdash; Canonical brand registry: the first piece of cross-tenant intelligence Refill carries.</strong> Grasshopper&rsquo;s architectural call (2026-06-01): instead of regex pattern-matching on service names (v1.29.4.x), maintain a curated database of aesthetics-industry brands the platform owns. CSV imports + recategorize sweeps match against display name + aliases. Adding a brand propagates to every tenant. Per <code>project_data_intelligence_thesis</code>: per-spa configuration in the foreground, cross-spa knowledge accumulating in the background. <strong>What ships (4 pieces)</strong>: (1) <code>supabase/migrations/20260601030000_v1_30_0_canonical_brands.sql</code> &mdash; new system-wide <code>canonical_brands</code> table with display_name + aliases[] + category + manufacturer + unit_type + notes, RLS read-allowed for authenticated / writes for service_role. (2) <strong>Seed of ~52 brands</strong>: Tox (5: Botox, Dysport, Xeomin, Jeuveau, Daxxify), Filler (22: full Juvederm Voluma/Vollure/Volbella/Ultra/Volux line + full Restylane Refyne/Defyne/Kysse/Lyft/Silk/Contour/Eyelight line + RHA Collection + Belotero + Radiesse + Sculptra + Versa), Laser (9: BBL/Halo/Moxi/Fraxel/CO2 Fractional/Thulium/IPL/Morpheus8/LHR), Skincare (12: SkinCeuticals C E Ferulic + Phloretin + EltaMD UV Clear/Daily/Sport + ZO + Obagi + Neocutis + Alastin + Revision + Anthelios), Facial (4: HydraFacial/Diamond Glow/AquaGold/Dermaplane). Each entry has a rich alias list (e.g. Voluma matches &ldquo;Voluma&rdquo;, &ldquo;Voluma XC&rdquo;, &ldquo;Juvederm Voluma&rdquo;, &ldquo;Juvederm Voluma XC&rdquo;). (3) <strong><code>lookupCanonicalBrand(name, brands)</code> matcher</strong> in <code>src/server/refill-catalog.ts</code>: flattens all aliases into pairs, sorts by alias length descending (most specific wins &mdash; &ldquo;Restylane Refyne&rdquo; beats &ldquo;Restylane&rdquo;), tests each as a case-insensitive word-boundary regex. First match wins. Returns null → caller falls back to existing regex inference. (4) <strong><code>recategorizeServicesFromBrandsFn</code> retroactive sweep</strong>: scans every existing service in the tenant, applies canonical lookup against name + notes, updates category where matched. Surfaced as a <strong>&ldquo;Re-categorize&rdquo; button</strong> on <code>/catalog/services</code> PageHeader (next to Import CSV + Add service). Karen&rsquo;s 85 &ldquo;Other&rdquo; rows get sorted into Tox / Filler / Laser / etc. without re-importing. <strong>Admin CRUD at <code>/app/admin/canonical-brands</code></strong>: full create / edit / delete UI with search box across display name + aliases, grouped by category, comma-separated alias input, manufacturer dropdown, category + unit-type pickers. Server fns gate on <code>app_role = &apos;admin&apos;</code>. <strong>What this unblocks</strong>: v1.30.1 will wire the canonical lookup into <code>ingestServicesCsvFn</code> (currently only applies on the retroactive sweep, not at import time) and bundle the products-CSV import path. v1.30.2 will add the &ldquo;Suggest new brand&rdquo; flow from import preview &mdash; unmatched names get queued for admin promotion. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: import-time canonical lookup (queued v1.30.1). Suggest-new-brand workflow. Tenant-level brand overrides. Auto-link product rows to canonical brands on products-CSV import. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>supabase/migrations/20260601030000_v1_30_0_canonical_brands.sql</code> (new, schema + seed), <code>src/server/refill-catalog.ts</code> (CanonicalBrand types + lookupCanonicalBrand + recategorizeServicesFromBrandsFn + listCanonicalBrandsFn + createCanonicalBrandFn + updateCanonicalBrandFn + deleteCanonicalBrandFn + requireAdmin helper), <code>src/routes/app.admin.canonical-brands.tsx</code> (new, ~480 lines admin CRUD with search + category grouping + alias chip rendering), <code>src/routes/app.refill.catalog.services.tsx</code> (Re-categorize button + onRecategorize handler), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
