      "<strong>v1.29.4.2 &mdash; QuickBooks reality check: 4 fixes after the first real Rejuv export.</strong> Per <code>feedback_validate_against_real_exports</code>: shipped v1.29.4 + .1 with educated guesses; the first real Karen-Rejuv QB Item List export surfaced 4 things the parser missed. <strong>(1) Title-row skip</strong>: QB prepends a company-name row (&ldquo;REJUV SKIN SPA, LLC,,,,&rdquo;) above the actual headers. v1.29.4 treated it as the header row, so 219/219 rows parsed as junk. New <code>findHeaderRowIndex</code> searches the first 8 lines for a row containing a recognizable name-column header and starts parsing from there. Preview now reports &ldquo;Skipped N preamble rows&rdquo; when this triggers. <strong>(2) QB-actual column aliases</strong>: <code>Product/Service full name</code> (the QB name column, leading alias now), <code>Purchase price</code> (QB&rsquo;s cost column &mdash; not &ldquo;Cost&rdquo;), <code>Memo/Description</code> (QB&rsquo;s description column). <strong>(3) Type-as-filter, not category</strong>: QB&rsquo;s Type column values are <code>Service</code> / <code>Non-inventory</code> / <code>Inventory</code> &mdash; these classify the ROW (service vs product), not the category. v1.29.4.1 had been (incorrectly) mapping Type into the category enum and falling back to name-inference when the values didn&rsquo;t match. v1.29.4.2 introduces <code>TYPE_HEADER_CANDIDATES</code> separate from <code>CATEGORY_HEADER_CANDIDATES</code> and the parser threads <code>isService</code> through every row. Category continues to come from name-inference (botox &rarr; tox, BBL &rarr; laser, HydraFacial &rarr; facial). <strong>(4) Skip non-service rows on commit</strong>: any row with Type matching Non-inventory / Inventory is now flagged as &ldquo;Skip (product)&rdquo; in the preview (amber chip, dimmed row) and excluded from the commit. These are retail items Karen resells &mdash; they belong in <code>/catalog/products</code> once the products-CSV path ships. Preview summary chip surfaces the skip count. <strong>UI changes</strong>: column mapping table gains a &ldquo;Service / Product type&rdquo; row; preview table gains a Type column; non-service rows render dimmed with a &ldquo;Skip (product)&rdquo; chip; commit button copy + disabled-logic counts only willCreate + willUpdate (not parseable total, since non-service rows are parseable but intentionally skipped). <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: the products-CSV import path (still queued; needs its own preview + commit + manufacturer-detection). Negative-price rows still default to $0 with a warning (Karen-fixable in services UI). Category inference doesn&rsquo;t look up product-affinity (a &ldquo;Belotero&rdquo; row currently maps to filler via the filler regex; if a product name is too generic, it lands in &lsquo;other&rsquo;). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/lib/catalog-csv.ts</code> (findHeaderRowIndex helper + TYPE_HEADER_CANDIDATES + new QB-leading aliases + isService flag + headerRowIndex + nonServiceRows count), <code>src/server/refill-catalog.ts</code> (ImportPreview gains type + headerRowIndex + nonServiceRows + willSkipNonService; commit skips non-service rows), <code>src/routes/app.refill.catalog.import.tsx</code> (Type row in mapping + skip-preamble note + Non-service summary chip + Type column in preview table + Skip chip + dimmed rows + commit count adjusted), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
