      "<strong>v1.29.4 &mdash; Service-list CSV import: preview-then-commit upsert by name.</strong> Closes the v1.29.x Catalog sprint. Drop your Acuity service-list export (or any CSV with a service-name column) at <code>/app/refill/catalog/import</code> &rarr; client reads the file &rarr; server parses + auto-detects columns + previews what would land &rarr; you eyeball it &rarr; Commit upserts. <strong>Per <code>feedback_validate_against_real_exports</code></strong>: this ships with the parser scaffolded against common Acuity column shapes (Name / Category / Price / Description / Duration variants), but is NOT claimed as &ldquo;Acuity-validated&rdquo; until the first real export has been dropped + iterated to clean. Synthetic fixtures are not validation; that&rsquo;s rule one. <strong>Parser (<code>src/lib/catalog-csv.ts</code>)</strong>: hand-rolled CSV tokenizer (handles quoted fields + escaped quotes + commas inside quotes) mirroring patient-csv style; fuzzy header matching with substring fallback; name-based category inference when the CSV has no category column (botox/dysport/jeuveau/daxxify &rarr; tox; juvederm/restylane/radiesse &rarr; filler; bbl/ipl/moxi/halo/fraxel/laser &rarr; laser; hydrafacial/peel/microderm/dermaplane &rarr; facial; skincare/serum/cleanser &rarr; skincare; default other); price parsing strips currency symbols + commas + whitespace. <strong>Server fn <code>ingestServicesCsvFn</code></strong>: single endpoint with <code>mode: &apos;preview&apos; | &apos;commit&apos;</code> &mdash; preview returns parse stats + field mapping + per-row preview with action (create / update) + warnings; commit re-parses (don&rsquo;t trust client) and upserts by name (case-insensitive within tenant scope). Re-uploading the same file is safe &mdash; no duplicates created. Failed rows surface in the receipt with row index + reason. <strong>UI (<code>app.refill.catalog.import.tsx</code>)</strong>: drag-drop dropzone or file picker; on file drop, automatic preview runs; column mapping table shows which CSV header maps to which field (with required-flag on Name); summary chips (Total / Parseable / Will create / Will update); preview table of first 30 rows with auto-detected category + &lsquo;(from name)&rsquo; / &lsquo;(default)&rsquo; chips when inferred; warnings inline per row; Import button disabled if no name column found (required gate). Receipt screen on commit success: created count, updated count, failed rows with reason, links to View services or Import another file. <strong>Discovery</strong>: &lsquo;Import CSV&rsquo; button added to <code>/app/refill/catalog/services</code> PageHeader next to &lsquo;Add service&rsquo; &mdash; first-class affordance, not buried. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: products CSV import (queued; needs manufacturer-portal export samples). Bulk re-categorize. Service-duration storage (parser reads the column, server ignores it &mdash; duration isn&rsquo;t stored on services yet). Import undo. Auto-link products to imported services (separate v1.x feature once products-CSV ships). <strong>The real-export validation cycle</strong>: when Grasshopper drops his Karen-Rejuv Acuity export, the column mapping table will show the actual headers in his file; if any are unmapped or misclassified, the parser learns the new alias and re-ships. No row writes until the parser shows green on his real data. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/lib/catalog-csv.ts</code> (new, ~260 lines parser), <code>src/server/refill-catalog.ts</code> (added ImportPreview + ImportReceipt types + ingestServicesCsvFn, ~160 lines), <code>src/routes/app.refill.catalog.import.tsx</code> (new, ~430 lines UI), <code>src/routes/app.refill.catalog.services.tsx</code> (Import CSV button in PageHeader), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no nav change beyond the Import button on Services page.",
