      "<strong>v1.29.1 &mdash; Products CRUD: the first UI surface on the Profitability Engine substrate.</strong> v1.29.0 shipped the schema; v1.29.1 lights it up. Surface at <code>/app/refill/catalog/products</code> &mdash; deep-link only per <code>project_refill_trojan_horse_thesis</code> (the 5-chip RefillNav stays narrow forever). <strong>What lands</strong>: <code>src/server/refill-catalog.ts</code> (new module) with four server fns &mdash; <code>listProductsFn</code>, <code>createProductFn</code>, <code>updateProductFn</code>, <code>deleteProductFn</code>. Auth pattern: <code>verifyAuth</code> &rarr; <code>resolveEffectiveUserId</code> (admin viewAs honored) &rarr; <code>getTenantIdForUser</code> &rarr; tenant-scoped query. Matches refill-billing.ts shape verbatim. <strong>UI</strong>: <code>src/routes/app.refill.catalog.products.tsx</code> renders products grouped by category (Tox / Filler / Laser consumable / Skincare / Other) with one card per product. Each card surfaces brand + unit-type chip + manufacturer chip + cost &rarr; sell &rarr; margin (auto-computed dollars + percentage). Click any card to edit in place; inline Add form expander at top; Delete with confirm at the bottom of the edit form. Empty state has a guided &ldquo;Add your first product&rdquo; CTA explaining that cost + sales price unlock margin math for the entire Profitability Engine. Mobile-responsive (Karen on her phone is the design target). <strong>Form details</strong>: brand + manufacturer dropdown (14 options including the AbbVie / former-Allergan label clarification) + category + unit-type + cost + sales-price + notes; margin preview block updates live as you type. Zod validation server-side; client guards numeric parsing. <strong>Architectural notes</strong>: (1) Server fns return camelCase typed <code>Product</code> objects with <code>marginPerUnit</code> + <code>marginPct</code> pre-computed (compute-in-app per spec). (2) tenant_id check on UPDATE and DELETE matches insert-policy pattern &mdash; defense-in-depth against an ID leak. (3) ProductManufacturer enum exported from <code>src/server/refill-catalog.ts</code> matches the 14 CHECK-constraint values from v1.29.0 migration verbatim. <strong>What this unblocks</strong>: v1.29.2 Services CRUD (structurally identical with a different table) and v1.29.3 service_products linkage + auto-margin derive. v1.29.4 Acuity CSV import per <code>feedback_validate_against_real_exports</code>. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: no nav-chip widening (per trojan-horse). No CSV import yet. No bulk-edit. No price-history (cost_per_unit / sales_price_per_unit are current-state-only). No tenant-customizable categories. <strong>Verification</strong>: log in to production &rarr; navigate to <code>/app/refill/catalog/products</code> &rarr; empty state renders &rarr; add a Botox 100u vial (AbbVie, cost $400, sell $1200) &rarr; row renders in Tox group with $800 margin (67%) &rarr; click to edit &rarr; change sell price to $1250 &rarr; save &rarr; reload &rarr; persisted. Test admin viewAs via PersonaSwitcher. <strong>Rollback</strong>: <code>git revert</code>; no DB damage (tables already exist from v1.29.0; new rows are tenant-scoped and deletable). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/server/refill-catalog.ts</code> (new file, ~250 lines), <code>src/routes/app.refill.catalog.products.tsx</code> (new file, ~430 lines), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no nav change.",
