      "<strong>v1.27.2 &mdash; Picker UI at <code>/app/refill/waitlist/invite</code> closes the v1.27.x Karen-go-live arc end-to-end.</strong> Surface where Karen actually does the work: pick A-list patients (default top 5 by lifetime spend, with Top 5 / 10 / 20 quick-selects), review + edit the invite copy with live token preview, hit Send. The button calls v1.27.1&rsquo;s <code>sendOptInInviteBatchFn</code> &mdash; the server pipeline drops one ready-to-send iMessage draft per patient into her inbox, Claude Desktop&rsquo;s MCP cron picks it up at the top of the hour and drafts each blue-bubble message in Messages.app for her to tap Send. Same delivery channel as the rescue dispatcher; different conversation (cold opt-in invite vs. live rescue offer). <strong>New file</strong>: <code>src/routes/app.refill.waitlist.invite.tsx</code>. Bootstrap loads in one parallel round: <code>listPatients</code> (full <code>PatientListRow</code> shape with phone/lifetimeSpend/banned/vip), <code>getMyAListRules</code> (saved A-list thresholds), <code>listReliabilityFlags</code> (cancellation/no-show counts for the exclude-unreliable rule), and the new <code>getInviteCopyTemplateFn</code> from v1.27.1 (per-tenant override or system default). Filters to phone-having patients that pass A-list rules, sorts by lifetime spend descending, auto-selects top 5 on first load. Editable textarea pre-fills from the saved template; live preview renders against the first selected patient with the four supported tokens substituted (<code>{first_name}</code>, <code>{owner_name}</code>, <code>{spa_name}</code>, <code>{opt_in_url}</code>). &lsquo;Save as default&rsquo; calls the existing <code>setSpaProfileLookupKeyFn</code> with <code>lookupKey=invite-copy-template</code> (v1.27.1 wired this through). Per-patient result table after send: Drafted / Already on waitlist / No phone / Banned/opted out / Error chips. <strong>A-list logic deduplication</strong>: <code>matchesRules</code> (12 lines, pure function) lifted out of <code>app.refill.patients.a-list-rules.tsx</code> into <code>src/lib/a-list-rules.ts</code> as <code>matchesAListRules</code>. Both routes now import from the same source &mdash; adding a field to <code>AListRules</code> in the future is a one-place change. <strong>Why no main-nav link</strong>: the four-chip Refill nav (Recovery / Inbox / Settings / Billing) is the &lsquo;narrow forever&rsquo; pillar from <code>project_refill_trojan_horse_thesis</code>. Waitlist surfaces stay deep-link-only for now, accessed via Karen-onboarding instructions or direct URL share. <strong>Why no link from waitlist/bulk to here</strong>: the two pages answer different questions &mdash; bulk = &lsquo;give me URLs to distribute through my own email blast / Mailchimp / patient-comm channel&rsquo;, invite = &lsquo;compose + send blue-bubble iMessages from my Apple ID&rsquo;. Cross-linking them would muddle the mental models. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T ship</strong>: inbound STOP/START keyword routing from iMessage MCP replies (v1.27.3 &mdash; the SMS handler in <code>emma-optout.functions.ts</code> already detects keywords; v1.27.3 wires it to a Claude-Desktop reply-pull bridge). Also doesn&rsquo;t backfill <code>viewAsUserId</code> on the legacy <code>bulkSeedWaitlistIntents</code> or <code>listSeedablePatients</code> (the v374 bulk page works fine when Karen logs in directly; admin viewing-as-Karen on the legacy bulk page is a separate cleanup, low priority since this new invite page covers Karen&rsquo;s production path). <strong>Verification path</strong>: testspaowner magic-link &rarr; <code>/app/refill/waitlist/invite</code> &rarr; confirm A-list candidates load + default top-5 selected + edit template + Save-as-default round-trips through Supabase + Send fires &rarr; check davidfand303@gmail.com for the proxy email &rarr; tap any opt-in URL in the email &rarr; lands on v1.27.0&rsquo;s public route &rarr; tap &lsquo;Yes, count me in&rsquo; &rarr; confirm <code>emma_waitlist.status='active'</code> + <code>opted_in_at</code> stamped via Supabase dashboard. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/routes/app.refill.waitlist.invite.tsx</code> (new file, the picker), <code>src/lib/a-list-rules.ts</code> (new file, the shared matcher), <code>src/routes/app.refill.patients.a-list-rules.tsx</code> (import + rename <code>matchesRules</code> &rarr; <code>matchesAListRules</code>; delete local copy), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration; no server-fn additions (all wiring built in v1.27.1).",
