    items: [
      "<strong>v1.27.1 &mdash; Outbound iMessage-MCP invite pipeline: <code>sendOptInInviteBatchFn</code> server fn + per-tenant editable invite-copy template.</strong> Second leg of the v1.27.x Karen-go-live arc. v1.27.0 closed the patient-side surface (<code>/waitlist/optin/&lt;token&gt;</code>). This ship gives Karen (and the v1.27.2 picker UI) a server pipeline that takes a list of patient_node_ids + an invite body, atomically creates paused <code>emma_waitlist</code> rows + mints tokens + composes a Karen-facing proxy email with per-patient ready-to-send iMessage drafts, then sends it via Resend to her <code>rescue_proxy_email</code> inbox. Claude Desktop&rsquo;s hourly cron picks up the email, calls <code>draft_imessage(recipient_phone, body)</code> via the imessage-draft MCP, drafts blue-bubble iMessages in Messages.app from Karen&rsquo;s Apple ID. Same delivery channel as the rescue dispatcher, but for cold opt-in invites instead of rescue offers. <strong>New file</strong>: <code>src/server/emma-waitlist-invite.functions.ts</code>. Exports <code>DEFAULT_INVITE_TEMPLATE</code> (Karen-toned default with <code>{first_name}</code>, <code>{owner_name}</code>, <code>{spa_name}</code>, <code>{opt_in_url}</code> tokens + TCPA &lsquo;Reply STOP&rsquo; footer), <code>sendOptInInviteBatchFn</code> (the pipeline), <code>getInviteCopyTemplateFn</code> (resolver returning override-or-default for the picker UI). <strong>Pipeline shape</strong>: resolve effective user id (viewAsUserId-aware from day 1 so admin-viewing-as-Karen works), load spa-profile bundle + rescue_proxy_email + patient metadata in parallel, then per-patient: upsert paused waitlist row (skip if status=&lsquo;active&rsquo;, with per-row result codes <code>sent / skipped_already_on_waitlist / skipped_no_phone / skipped_banned_or_opted_out / error</code>) + mint stable token via existing <code>getOrMintWaitlistToken</code> + render body with token substitutions. Compose proxy email mirroring <code>composeProxyEmail</code> from <code>emma-rescue.functions.ts</code>:463-547 (AUTO-SEND directive at top, one section per patient, paste-into-Claude-Desktop framing). Send via Resend with <code>type=refill-waitlist-invite</code> tag for downstream telemetry. If Resend fails, every <code>sent</code> row downgrades to <code>error</code> with the failure message attached &mdash; no silent successes when the email never landed. <strong>Per-tenant invite copy</strong>: extends <code>emma-spa-profile.ts</code>&rsquo;s <code>SpaProfileLookupKey</code> union + <code>SpaProfileBundle</code> shape to include <code>invite-copy-template</code> as a fourth scalar (joins spa-name, owner-display-name, from-number in the same <code>knowledge_nodes</code> bucket). Wired through <code>spa-profile.functions.ts</code>&rsquo;s <code>setInput</code> enum so the existing <code>setSpaProfileLookupKeyFn</code> can write it &mdash; v1.27.2 picker UI gets a free &lsquo;Save as default&rsquo; surface with no new server fn. <strong>Why a new file instead of extending emma-waitlist-seed</strong>: <code>bulkSeedWaitlistIntents</code> (v374) does the upsert + token side already but exposes URLs in a result table for manual distribution. This pipeline ALSO composes + sends the iMessage proxy email; the two functions answer different questions (&lsquo;mint URLs&rsquo; vs. &lsquo;send invites&rsquo;). Folding would&rsquo;ve made bulkSeed&rsquo;s signature schizophrenic. Keeping them separate keeps each call site clear about what it&rsquo;s asking for. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T ship</strong>: the picker UI itself (v1.27.2 &mdash; <code>/app/refill/waitlist/invite</code> with A-list filter + editable textarea + Save-as-default + send button), inbound STOP/START keyword routing from iMessage MCP replies (v1.27.3 &mdash; the <code>detectInboundKeyword</code> handler in <code>emma-optout.functions.ts</code> exists for SMS already; v1.27.3 wires it to a Claude-Desktop reply-pull bridge), <code>viewAsUserId</code> backfill on the legacy <code>bulkSeedWaitlistIntents</code> + <code>listSeedablePatients</code> (v1.27.2 prereq &mdash; rolling into that ship), and audit columns on <code>emma_waitlist</code> for what Karen actually sent (deferred unless v1.27.2 walk surfaces a need). <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/server/emma-waitlist-invite.functions.ts</code> (new file, the pipeline), <code>src/server/emma-spa-profile.ts</code> (extend <code>SpaProfileLookupKey</code> + <code>SpaProfileBundle</code> + <code>getSpaProfileBundle</code> for the fourth scalar), <code>src/server/spa-profile.functions.ts</code> (extend <code>setInput.lookupKey</code> enum), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration &mdash; <code>emma_waitlist</code>, <code>emma_waitlist_tokens</code>, and the spa-profile partial unique index all exist.",
    ],
