      "<strong>v1.26.21 &mdash; Rename the dormant tenant&rsquo;s spa-name so it can&rsquo;t be mistaken for an active one in the v1.26.20 admin banner.</strong> v1.26.20 made the admin defaulted-vs-explicit landing visible: when admin opens getrefill.app with no PersonaSwitcher pick, the amber-bright banner reads &lsquo;Defaulted to <em>tenant.name</em>&rsquo;. For the dormant tenant (auth identity <code>dormantspaowner@test.com</code>, user_id <code>ecf8bcee&hellip;57fc</code>, holds 5,754 historical Acuity appointments + 1,140 QB-uploaded patients but the recovery engine has never fired here) the <code>public.tenants.name</code> column held the bare string &lsquo;Rejuv&rsquo; &mdash; visually indistinguishable from an active spa. The v1.26.16 changelog flagged this as a data hygiene fix; v1.26.20 made it customer-visible (where &lsquo;customer&rsquo; here = Grasshopper-as-admin, the only persona who hits the banner). <strong>What shipped</strong>: a single-row data migration at <code>supabase/migrations/20260621010000_v126_21_dormant_spa_name_hygiene.sql</code> that UPDATEs <code>public.tenants.name</code> for the dormant tenant&rsquo;s row to &lsquo;[Dormant] Rejuv Skin Spa&rsquo;. Tenant resolution joins through <code>tenant_memberships</code> (the tenants table has no <code>owner_user_id</code>; ownership lives in memberships with <code>role='owner'</code>). <strong>Why this name and not &lsquo;dormantspaowner-stub&rsquo;</strong>: the leading <code>[Dormant]</code> tag is unmistakable to an admin glancing at the banner, but preserving the historical &lsquo;Rejuv Skin Spa&rsquo; phrase keeps the connection to Karen Aslakson&rsquo;s original spa readable rather than discarded into a robot identifier. Memory tag for the dormant tenant&rsquo;s history stays load-bearing. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: the dormant tenant&rsquo;s historical data (5,754 appointments, 1,140 patients, all Acuity-ingested in 2026-Q1 before the v417 routing flip) still sits in the dormant user&rsquo;s rows. Sweeping or archiving that data is a separate pre-launch decision per [[feedback-test-data-cleanup-deferred]] &mdash; defer to a single sweep. Also doesn&rsquo;t address the underlying <code>getFirstTenantForAdmin</code> ordering question (why is the dormant tenant served first when admin defaults? creation-order? alphabetic?) &mdash; that&rsquo;s a separate v1.27 candidate flagged in v1.26.20&rsquo;s notes. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>supabase/migrations/20260621010000_v126_21_dormant_spa_name_hygiene.sql</code> (new file, the data fix), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). Pure data fix; no code change to the running worker. Apply via Supabase dashboard SQL editor.",
