      "<strong>v1.26.18 &mdash; Close the <code>phone_numbers</code> schema-vs-code gap by reading the SMS from-number out of <code>knowledge_nodes</code> instead.</strong> Three near-duplicate <code>resolveSpaFromNumber</code> implementations (one each in <code>emma-rescue.functions.ts</code>, <code>emma-preshow.functions.ts</code>, <code>emma-blast.functions.ts</code>) all queried <code>phone_numbers</code> &mdash; a vestigial table from the Liz CRM that Refill cleaved away from and that never existed in this schema. At runtime the Supabase client returned an error on the missing table; <code>.maybeSingle()</code> swallowed it to null. Karen&rsquo;s engine still fired because she&rsquo;s in pure proxy-email mode (<code>rescue_proxy_email = davidfand303@gmail.com</code>, no <code>rescue_proxy_phone</code>), so the <code>willNeedFromNumber</code> gate skipped the requirement entirely. Any spa wanting direct SMS or proxy-SMS-to-owner would have hit &lsquo;Spa has no provisioned SMS number&rsquo; with no working configuration path. <strong>Three paths considered</strong>: (A) read from <code>knowledge_nodes</code> spa-profile pattern (matches the v1.26.12 <code>owner-display-name</code> shape, no migration), (B) create a real <code>phone_numbers</code> table (the original framing &mdash; mirrors a vestigial pattern for one value per tenant with no admin UI), (C) delete the function and lock Refill to proxy-email-only (too lossy). <strong>Shipping A.</strong> spa-profile is the established tenant-config bucket; storing from-number alongside spa-name + hours + address + owner-display-name keeps one mental model + one settings surface. <strong>Code change</strong>: each <code>resolveSpaFromNumber</code> body swaps the table from <code>phone_numbers</code> to <code>knowledge_nodes</code>, filters <code>context = 'spa-profile'</code> + <code>lookup_key = 'from-number'</code>, returns <code>title</code> trimmed (matches the read pattern <code>resolveSpaName</code> and <code>resolveOwnerDisplayName</code> already use in the same files). Signatures unchanged so call sites need no edits. <strong>How a spa wires up direct SMS going forward</strong>: one SQL row in <code>knowledge_nodes</code> with <code>(user_id, context='spa-profile', lookup_key='from-number', title='+12085551234')</code>, same shape as the v1.26.12 owner-display-name override. Settings UI for editing this is a v1.27 candidate alongside the owner-display-name editor. <strong>Why per-tenant scalar in knowledge_nodes, not a new table</strong>: a real <code>phone_numbers</code> table would buy multi-row support (one-spa-many-numbers, is_active flag, sort by created_at) the original Liz CRM had, but Refill&rsquo;s code already collapses to <code>.limit(1).maybeSingle()</code> &mdash; v1 is one number per tenant. New table for one scalar is overengineering relative to the existing spa-profile pattern. <strong>What this DOESN&rsquo;T fix</strong>: the three near-duplicate <code>resolveSpaFromNumber</code> implementations are still copy-pasted across emma-rescue + emma-preshow + emma-blast (same duplication exists for <code>resolveSpaName</code> in 2 files + <code>resolveOwnerDisplayName</code> in 1, all reading spa-profile). Folding into a shared <code>emma-spa-profile.ts</code> helper is a future DRY pass &mdash; out of scope for closing the phone_numbers gap. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/server/emma-rescue.functions.ts</code> (helper body swap + architectural comment), <code>src/server/emma-preshow.functions.ts</code> (helper body swap), <code>src/server/emma-blast.functions.ts</code> (helper body swap + docblock refresh), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry). No migration.",
