      "<strong>v1.26.15 &mdash; Strip Acuity&rsquo;s baked-in provider name from rescue treatment labels.</strong> Surfaced during v1.26.12 verification: Karen&rsquo;s Acuity calendar uses treatment strings like <code>Tox w/ Karen</code> and <code>Filler with Karen</code>, where the provider name is welded into the treatment label itself. Every rescue surface (claim page, rescue SMS, proxy SMS, proxy email) <em>also</em> appends its own <code> with &lt;provider&gt;</code> clause via <code>providerClause</code> (composers) and <code>displayProviderName</code> (claim page). Result on Karen&rsquo;s tenant: SMS reads <code>... for Tox w/ Karen with Karen</code>; claim page renders headline <code>an opening just came up with Karen</code> + Treatment row <code>Tox w/ Karen</code> + With row <code>Karen</code> &mdash; three repeats of the same name on one card. Naming the wrong claim: v1.26.12 added the &lsquo;with Karen&rsquo; warmth signal assuming the treatment label was a clean noun phrase. It isn&rsquo;t for solo-practitioner Acuity setups &mdash; the provider name is already part of the label. <strong>Fix</strong>: new <code>stripProviderFromTreatment(treatment, providerName, ownerDisplayName)</code> helper sitting next to <code>providerClause</code>. Strips trailing <code>&lt;connector&gt; &lt;candidate&gt;</code> where connector is one of <code>w/</code>, <code>with</code>, <code>-</code>, <code>&ndash;</code>, <code>&mdash;</code>, <code>/</code>, <code>:</code> and candidate is the provider name or the spa-profile owner-display-name (case-insensitive). Anchored to <code>$</code> so it only catches trailing bake-ins &mdash; <code>Consultation</code> and <code>30 min facial</code> pass through untouched. Returns the original string if stripping would empty it. <strong>Applied at the four sites</strong> that hold treatment + provider + owner together: <code>composeRescueSms</code>, <code>composeProxySms</code>, <code>composeProxyEmail</code>, and <code>getRescueOfferPayload</code> (so the claim-page UI receives a pre-cleaned <code>treatmentType</code> &mdash; Treatment row and SMS body source the same cleaned value). <strong>Effect on Karen&rsquo;s tenant</strong>: SMS becomes <code>... for Tox with Karen</code> (single render). Claim page reads <code>an opening just came up with Karen</code> + Treatment <code>Tox</code> + With <code>Karen</code> &mdash; three slots, three pieces of information, no repeat. <strong>Multi-practitioner spas</strong> (Acuity calendar named after provider, not practice): labels without a trailing provider token pass through unchanged; <code>providerClause</code> render still works the same. <strong>Why strip-on-read, not re-prompt spas</strong>: re-asking the practice to clean their Acuity treatment library is unreasonable &mdash; those labels are what the team has been typing for years and they shouldn&rsquo;t have to re-do data entry to look right in our UI. Strip on render, leave the source-of-truth alone. <strong>Touched</strong>: <code>src/server/emma-rescue.functions.ts</code> (helper + 4 apply sites + 1 <code>resolvedOwnerDisplayName</code> local for reuse in the payload return), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
