      "<strong>v1.26.8 &mdash; Impersonation sweep: emma-attribution + emma-deposits, plus recovery dashboard full impersonation correctness.</strong> The recovery dashboard (<code>/app/refill/recovery</code>) was the page that v1.26.7 explicitly left half-done &mdash; <code>getInvoicePreview</code> got swept on the server side, but the route was untouched to avoid the split-brain UI where one card shows tenant data while three others show admin&rsquo;s empty bucket. This ship closes the remaining files and flips all four reads + three writes in one consistent change. <strong>emma-attribution.functions.ts &mdash; 4 gaps closed</strong>: <code>listRecoveryEvents</code> (line 239 read; admin saw their own empty <code>emma_recovery_events</code> bucket instead of Karen&rsquo;s verified events), <code>getRecoveryStats</code> (line 405 read; MoM math + month/lifetime totals + provisional count all came back zero under impersonation), <code>manualConfirmRecovery</code> (line 336 write; admin clicking Confirm on Karen&rsquo;s page would silently no-op because the <code>.eq(&apos;user_id&apos;, userId)</code> filter targeted admin&rsquo;s empty bucket; <code>verified_by</code> would also have logged admin&rsquo;s id if the row existed). <code>unconfirmRecovery</code> (line 383 write; same silent no-op pattern for undo). <strong>emma-deposits.functions.ts &mdash; 2 gaps closed</strong>: <code>listDepositIntents</code> (line 212 read; deposits tab empty under impersonation), <code>markDepositVoided</code> (line 267 write; void silently no-op&rsquo;d while Karen&rsquo;s deposit stayed visible). <strong>Internal helpers explicitly excluded</strong>: <code>recordRecoveryEvent</code>, <code>reconcileRecoveryEventsForUser</code> (attribution), <code>checkDepositEligibility</code>, <code>logDepositIntent</code> (deposits) &mdash; all take <code>userId</code> as a direct arg from caller; not <code>createServerFn</code>, no HTTP surface, caller-validated. <strong>All 6 schemas extended</strong>: <code>listInput</code> (attribution), <code>manualInput</code>, <code>unconfirmInput</code>, <code>statsInput</code> (attribution), <code>listInput</code> (deposits), <code>voidInput</code> (deposits) &mdash; each adds <code>viewAsUserId: z.string().uuid().optional()</code>. <code>verifyAuth</code> import removed from both files (no remaining callers). <strong>Recovery route plumbing</strong>: <code>app.refill.recovery.tsx</code> now imports <code>useTenantMembership</code> + derives <code>viewAsUserId</code> + threads it through <strong>seven</strong> call sites (the 4 attribution reads/writes, 2 deposit reads/writes, plus the previously-swept <code>getInvoicePreview</code>). <code>load</code> useCallback&rsquo;s dep array updated to include <code>viewAsUserId</code> so a mid-session admin switching from one tenant to another triggers a refresh instead of showing stale prior-tenant data. <strong>Audit fields</strong>: <code>verified_by</code> (manualConfirmRecovery) and <code>voided_by</code> (markDepositVoided) now record the <em>effective</em> user_id (impersonated tenant), matching the established v1.25.6 / v1.26.6 / v1.26.7 pattern. Attribution-back-to-admin (&lsquo;who really clicked&rsquo;) would need a separate <code>actor_user_id</code> column &mdash; not in scope. <strong>What this means for Karen</strong>: an admin can now walk Karen&rsquo;s entire recovery dashboard end-to-end via the persona switcher and see her real numbers (MoM math, treatment breakdown, deposit intents, invoice preview) instead of an empty admin bucket. Confirm / undo / void all land in Karen&rsquo;s data, not admin&rsquo;s. The [VERIFIED] math discipline that this page exists to demonstrate now actually works under the surface admin uses to debug it. <strong>Sweep series status after tonight</strong>: 8 ships across the impersonation work (v1.25.5/.6, v1.26.1, v1.26.6, v1.26.7, v1.26.8) closed 17 raw-verifyAuth gaps across 7 files. emma-rescue scouted clean. emma-billing has 3 dead-code fns still on verifyAuth (intentionally left for the emma&harr;refill unification cleanup ship). Still-untouched server files have either no impersonation surface (no createServerFn, internal helpers only) or have not been audited &mdash; the next regression that surfaces &lsquo;zero rows under impersonation&rsquo; will name the next target. Touched: <code>src/server/emma-attribution.functions.ts</code> (4 schemas + 4 handlers + verifyAuth import removal), <code>src/server/emma-deposits.functions.ts</code> (2 schemas + 2 handlers + verifyAuth import removal), <code>src/routes/app.refill.recovery.tsx</code> (useTenantMembership import + viewAsUserId derivation + 7 call sites + load dep array), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
