      "<strong>v1.26.7 &mdash; Impersonation sweep: billing files. Plus a naming-collision discovery + scope-discipline call.</strong> Final pair of files in tonight&rsquo;s impersonation-sweep series (emma-appointments v1.25.5/.6, rep-platform v1.26.1, emma-reliability v1.26.6, emma-rescue v1.26.5 scout&rsquo;d clean). Two parallel background Explore scouts catalogued <code>emma-billing.functions.ts</code> + <code>refill-billing.ts</code>. First-pass reports flagged ~6 gaps across both files &mdash; on verification, only <strong>2 were live</strong>; the others were either dead-code (emma&harr;refill fork left legacy exports stranded per v1.7.2), intentional caller-keyed for security (<code>getPaymentMethodStatus</code> &mdash; admin must NOT see tenant&rsquo;s Stripe payment method), or webhook/cron entries (no user-auth surface). <strong>Naming collision caught</strong>: both files export <code>applyPricingPlan</code>, <code>getActivePlan</code>, <code>listInvoices</code>, <code>getInvoicePreview</code> with identical names but different bodies. Each scout assumed its file was the called one; verification against actual import paths in routes resolved the ambiguity: <code>app.billing.tsx</code> imports the four plan/invoice fns from <code>refill-billing</code> (per v1.7.2&rsquo;s emma&rarr;refill migration), and <code>app.refill.recovery.tsx</code> imports <code>getInvoicePreview</code> from <code>emma-billing.functions</code> (the migration only swept billing.tsx, not recovery.tsx). So emma-billing&rsquo;s applyPricingPlan/getActivePlan/listInvoices have zero live call sites &mdash; legacy code from before the refill-billing fork &mdash; and refill-billing&rsquo;s getInvoicePreview is also dead (only emma-billing&rsquo;s is wired). <strong>The two live gaps closed</strong>: <code>refill-billing.ts:applyPricingPlan</code> at line 170 (write-path; admin impersonating Karen would insert the new <code>refill_pricing_plans</code> row keyed to admin&rsquo;s user_id, then update <code>tenants.plan</code> on the WRONG tenant via <code>getTenantIdForUser(admin)</code> &mdash; or fail outright if admin has no tenant). <code>emma-billing.functions.ts:getInvoicePreview</code> at line 382 (read-path; recovery dashboard MTD math would compute off admin&rsquo;s empty <code>emma_pricing_plans</code> + <code>emma_recovery_events</code> buckets). Both schemas extended with <code>viewAsUserId: z.string().uuid().optional()</code>; both handlers swap <code>verifyAuth</code> for <code>resolveEffectiveUserId</code>. <code>app.billing.tsx:231</code> applyPricingPlan call site updated to pass <code>viewAsUserId</code> from the existing <code>useTenantMembership</code> hook (already wired at line 97). <strong>v1.20 framing reversal noted</strong>: v1.20 explicitly excluded applyPricingPlan from the viewAsUserId opt-in (&lsquo;admin shouldn&rsquo;t be inadvertently mutating the impersonated tenant&rsquo;s plan&rsquo;). Subsequent sweeps (v1.25.5 ingestPatientCsv, v1.26.1 ensureMyRepAccount) established that mutation paths under impersonation are SAFE as long as admin&rsquo;s intent is explicit (clicking through the persona-switched UI is intent enough). Closing applyPricingPlan now in alignment with that established pattern. <strong>Recovery route NOT touched &mdash; scope discipline</strong>: <code>app.refill.recovery.tsx</code> calls four server fns &mdash; <code>getInvoicePreview</code> (now impersonation-capable) plus <code>listRecoveryEvents</code> + <code>getRecoveryStats</code> (emma-attribution.functions.ts, not in tonight&rsquo;s scope) + <code>listDepositIntents</code> (emma-deposits.functions.ts, also not in scope). Wiring useTenantMembership + viewAsUserId for ONLY getInvoicePreview would create the split-brain UI that v1.25.6 warned about (invoice math shows Karen&rsquo;s data, recovery events show admin&rsquo;s empty bucket &mdash; harder to debug than complete failure). Leaving recovery.tsx untouched until emma-attribution + emma-deposits get scouted/swept; flip them all at once. Handler-side fix in this ship is still useful: collapses to verifyAuth path when no viewAsUserId is passed, so no regression to current state. <strong>Dead-code annotation</strong>: emma-billing&rsquo;s applyPricingPlan/getActivePlan/listInvoices + refill-billing&rsquo;s getInvoicePreview are dead and intentionally NOT fixed in this sweep &mdash; separate cleanup ship should decide delete-vs-migrate. v1.7.2 changelog already flagged the emma&harr;refill unification as backlog. <strong>verifyAuth import retained in emma-billing.functions</strong>: still used by the three legacy/dead fns. Will be removable when those are deleted or migrated. <strong>Remaining sweep targets after tonight</strong>: emma-attribution.functions.ts (listRecoveryEvents + getRecoveryStats) and emma-deposits.functions.ts (listDepositIntents) &mdash; flagged via the recovery-route split-brain analysis. Closing both will unblock recovery.tsx&rsquo;s full impersonation correctness. Touched: <code>src/server/refill-billing.ts</code> (applyPlanInput + applyPricingPlan handler), <code>src/server/emma-billing.functions.ts</code> (invoicePreviewInput new schema + getInvoicePreview handler + resolveEffectiveUserId import), <code>src/routes/app.billing.tsx</code> (viewAsUserId on applyPricingPlan call site), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
