      "<strong>v1.26.6 &mdash; Impersonation sweep: emma-reliability.functions.ts.</strong> Continuing the sweep pattern from v1.25.5/.6 (emma-appointments &mdash; 6 gaps closed), v1.26.1 (rep-platform &mdash; 2 gaps), and tonight&rsquo;s scout of emma-rescue (clean). Background Explore agent audit of <code>emma-reliability.functions.ts</code> found two raw-<code>verifyAuth</code> gaps and three clean fns. <strong>The two gaps</strong>: <code>dismissPatternAlert</code> at line 452 (admin impersonating Karen would update the alert row keyed to admin&rsquo;s own user_id &mdash; the <code>.eq(&apos;user_id&apos;, userId)</code> guard meant the dismiss silently no-op&rsquo;d against admin&rsquo;s empty bucket while Karen&rsquo;s alert stayed undismissed in the UI). <code>getReliabilityCard</code> at line 470 (per-patient detail read, no current call sites &mdash; declared for the future patient profile feature &mdash; but closing the gap now bakes correct semantics in before any UI consumes it, since a UI ship will plausibly land before the next sweep). <strong>The three clean fns confirmed</strong>: <code>listPatternAlerts</code> (already on <code>resolveEffectiveUserId</code> since v1.23.0), <code>recomputeReliabilityForPatient</code> (internal helper taking <code>userId</code> as a direct arg, correctness keyed to caller), <code>listReliabilityFlags</code> (just touched in v1.26.4/.5, already on <code>resolveEffectiveUserId</code>). <strong>Implementation</strong>: both <code>dismissInput</code> + <code>cardInput</code> zod schemas extended with <code>viewAsUserId: z.string().uuid().optional()</code>. Both handlers now thread <code>resolveEffectiveUserId({ accessToken, viewAsUserId })</code> and use <code>effectiveUserId</code> on the table eq + (for dismiss) the <code>dismissed_by</code> audit field. Call site at <code>app.refill.rescue.tsx:163</code> (<code>dismissAlert</code> handler) updated to pass <code>viewAsUserId</code> &mdash; the route already had <code>useTenantMembership</code> wired since v1.23.0 P3 sweep, so the variable was already in scope. <code>verifyAuth</code> is no longer imported from <code>@/server/auth-helpers</code> in this file (only <code>resolveEffectiveUserId</code> remains). <strong>Audit-trail caveat</strong>: <code>dismissed_by</code> now records the <em>effective</em> user_id (the impersonated tenant), not the admin who actually clicked. That matches the established pattern from v1.25.6 (impersonation is meant to be invisible to the tenant&rsquo;s data), but if attribution-back-to-admin ever matters for audit purposes (&lsquo;who really clicked dismiss&rsquo;) a separate <code>actor_user_id</code> column would be the right shape. Not in scope tonight. <strong>Remaining sweep targets</strong>: emma-billing.functions.ts, refill-billing.functions.ts &mdash; both untouched by tonight&rsquo;s scouts. Touched: <code>src/server/emma-reliability.functions.ts</code> (verifyAuth import removed, dismissInput + cardInput extended, both handlers swapped to resolveEffectiveUserId), <code>src/routes/app.refill.rescue.tsx</code> (viewAsUserId threaded at dismissAlert call site), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
