    items: [
      "<strong>v1.25.1 &mdash; A-list automation dashboard. Karen stops starring patients one-at-a-time; she sets rules and the platform does the bulk-mark in one round trip.</strong> Spa-owner-facing power surface at <code>/app/refill/patients/a-list-rules</code>, reachable from a third top-right link on the patients page (next to Contacts + Import CSV). NOT promoted into the chip nav &mdash; per the steering-wheel rule (<code>project_three_agent_architecture</code>) Refill platform defaults stay narrow; A-list automation is a power-user lever, not a configure-me default. <strong>Rules form</strong>: three sliders (lifetime spend &ge; $X, last visit within Y days, total visits &ge; Z) each with an on/off toggle so a rule can be disabled, plus an exclude-banned toggle. Defaults: $1,000 / 365 days / 3 visits / banned excluded. <strong>Live preview card</strong>: pure client-side filter against the already-loaded <code>PatientListRow[]</code> (every field needed &mdash; <code>lifetimeSpendUsd</code>, <code>lastVisit</code>, <code>totalVisits</code>, <code>banned</code> &mdash; was already baked into <code>knowledge_nodes.attachments</code> by the ingest pipeline). Instant slider feedback, no debounce, no RPC per drag. Card surfaces three counts: already A-list (matches AND currently VIP), would be added (matches AND not yet VIP &mdash; what Apply will write), manual stars preserved (currently VIP AND don't match &mdash; explicit reassurance the design-call protects manual work). <strong>Apply is ADDITIVE ONLY</strong>: ships writes vip=true on the addIds delta, never sets vip=false. Manual stars set via the per-row VIP toggle survive every Apply. The Plan-agent pushback on the original spec called this out as the biggest design footgun &mdash; Karen manually stars Mrs. Patel, runs rules tomorrow with spend&ge;$1k excluding Mrs. Patel, the silent-unstar wipes the intent without naming who. Additive-only sidesteps the manual-vs-rule-provenance problem entirely without a data-shape change. <strong>Clear is the separate destructive escape hatch</strong>: typed-confirm modal (must type CLEAR) that bulk-removes ALL vip flags including manual ones. Rules stay saved &mdash; re-apply rebuilds in one click. <strong>Bulk write path</strong>: new Postgres RPC <code>refill_bulk_set_vip(p_user_id, p_add_ids, p_remove_ids)</code> using <code>jsonb_set(attachments, '{vip}', 'true', true)</code> &mdash; merges the vip field without clobbering the rest of the PatientSummary blob (lifetimeSpend, lastVisit, productMix, loyaltyEngagement all live in the same jsonb). One round trip for a 1,140-row apply vs. 1,140 round trips if the per-row <code>setPatientVip</code> were looped. <strong>Persistence</strong>: extended <code>user_preferences</code> with a generic <code>prefs jsonb</code> column (room for future per-user settings without per-feature migrations). Rules stored under <code>prefs.aListRules</code>, lastAppliedAt under <code>prefs.aListLastAppliedAt</code>. <strong>Tenant impersonation safety</strong>: both new server fns (<code>getMyAListRules</code>, <code>saveAListRulesAndMarkApplied</code>) AND the new bulk write (<code>setPatientVipBulk</code>) go through <code>resolveEffectiveUserId</code> so an admin viewing-as Karen writes to Karen's row, not the admin's. The existing per-row <code>setPatientVip</code> (v385.2 legacy) intentionally left as-is &mdash; pre-existing gap, separate ship. <strong>Migration paste path</strong>: <code>supabase/migrations/20260528000000_user_preferences_prefs_jsonb.sql</code> &mdash; ALTER + CREATE FUNCTION + GRANT + NOTIFY in one file with verify queries inlined as comments at the bottom. Touched: <code>supabase/migrations/20260528000000_user_preferences_prefs_jsonb.sql</code> (new), <code>src/integrations/supabase/types.ts</code> (prefs column + refill_bulk_set_vip RPC types), <code>src/server/user-prefs.functions.ts</code> (AListRules type + DEFAULT_A_LIST_RULES + getMyAListRules + saveAListRulesAndMarkApplied), <code>src/server/patient-ingest.functions.ts</code> (setPatientVipBulk + setVipBulkInput), <code>src/routes/app.refill.patients.a-list-rules.tsx</code> (new route + RuleRow + StatChip + apply/clear modals), <code>src/routes/app.refill.patients.index.tsx</code> (third top-right link), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
    ],
