      "<strong>v1.21 &mdash; /claim-your-business ported from openagenticv4 with Refill-flavored cleave.</strong> Final P1 item from the <code>Agentiport-Port-Audit.html</code> deliverable. The marketing-landing CTA at <code>src/routes/index.tsx:248</code> has been linking to <code>/claim-your-business</code> for weeks, dead-routing 404. v1.21 lands the page. <strong>Strategic call during port</strong>: the source file (979 lines) was Emma-shaped &mdash; Agentiport header brand, Sparkles logo, &lsquo;Emma handles texts&rsquo; ValueProps, &lsquo;Emma is on standby&rsquo; footer, &lsquo;Hosted Messaging activation&rsquo; concept throughout, <code>/app/karen</code> destination link. Verbatim copy would have shipped 4-5 Emma user-facing violations + a 404 destination link. Instead, cleaved to Refill thesis: scrape&rarr;review&rarr;claim arc preserved (server fns + DB substrate unchanged), but every Emma reference translated to Refill voice anchored to the no-show-recovery loop. <strong>Header</strong>: Agentiport+Sparkles &rarr; Refill+&lsquo;R&rsquo; logo block matching <code>RefillShellChrome</code>, &lsquo;/ no-show recovery&rsquo; subtitle. <strong>H1</strong>: &lsquo;Meet your AI front desk&rsquo; &rarr; &lsquo;Turn your cancellations into recovered revenue.&rsquo; <strong>ValueProps (3 cards)</strong>: completely rewritten &mdash; Calendar/&lsquo;Refill watches your calendar&rsquo;, ShieldCheck/&lsquo;You only pay on what comes back&rsquo;, Sparkles/&lsquo;Your waitlist becomes your safety net&rsquo;. Anchors the pricing-killshot framing (free + % of recovered) directly on the landing surface. <strong>Stage 4 Done copy</strong>: &lsquo;Emma has your services loaded into her sandbox&rsquo; &rarr; &lsquo;Your services, hours, and policies are loaded into your Refill tenant. Recovery starts the moment you wire your scheduler and waitlist.&rsquo; &lsquo;What&rsquo;s next&rsquo; list rewritten: (1) wire scheduler (Acuity, Boulevard, Mindbody), (2) import patient list, (3) watch live recovery feed &mdash; matches the actual Refill onboarding path, not Emma&rsquo;s Hosted Messaging coordination story. <strong>Destination link</strong>: <code>/app/karen</code> &rarr; <code>/app/refill</code>. <strong>Footer</strong>: Agentiport+Emma copy &rarr; &lsquo;Refill · No-show recovery for spas.&rsquo; <strong>Stripped from imports</strong>: Briefcase (unused), MessageCircle (was for &lsquo;Emma handles texts&rsquo; ValueProp, no longer applicable), Plus (unused after rewrite), X (unused after rewrite). <strong>Styling switch</strong>: every Tailwind brand-token class converted to inline <code>style={{ ... }}</code> with hex literals matching <code>styles.css</code> @theme &mdash; defensive against any remaining silently-broken-token edge cases the v1.20.7 audit might have missed (same pattern <code>LiveRecoveryFeed</code> uses). <strong>Auto-save + resume-via-?session=&lt;id&gt; behavior preserved</strong>: 1500ms debounced <code>updateSpaScrape</code>, first-render skip, &lsquo;Saving…&rsquo;/&lsquo;Saved.&rsquo; indicator, full UUID hydration on mount, polling tick for in-flight scrapes. <strong>Components ported</strong>: <code>src/components/PasswordInput.tsx</code> (47 lines, mechanical copy) &mdash; was a transitive dep needed by the sign-up form. <strong>Server-fn deps already in refill-app</strong>: <code>startSpaScrape</code>, <code>getSpaClaimStatus</code>, <code>claimSpa</code>, <code>updateSpaScrape</code> in <code>src/server/spa-claim.functions.ts</code> (1500+ lines, ported earlier). <strong>ServicesEditCard component already ported</strong>. <strong>What this unblocks</strong>: the dead index.tsx CTA now lands somewhere real; an actual spa owner can paste their URL, see what we know, and claim &mdash; converging on the dashboard at <code>/app/refill</code> without ever seeing Agentiport/Emma branding. Funnel-critical surface restored. Touched: <code>src/routes/claim-your-business.tsx</code> (new, ~700 lines), <code>src/components/PasswordInput.tsx</code> (new), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
