      "<strong>v1.13 &mdash; /start page ported from openagenticv4 (P0 audit fix, ship 2 of the port sprint).</strong> Per the <code>Agentiport-Port-Audit.html</code> finding, <code>/start</code> was the missing P0 landing page for the cold-email funnel: every Karen variant&rsquo;s &lsquo;Set up Refill for my spa&rsquo; CTA points here, and without it the funnel landed at a 404 between /scan and /onboard. Now live: thin manual-intake form capturing the minimum Karen + David need to onboard a new spa within 24 hours &mdash; practice name, email, scheduler dropdown (25 schedulers including Acuity / Boulevard / Mangomint / Mindbody / GlossGenius / etc), plus optional phone + estimated monthly cancels + freeform notes. Why manual not self-serve: shipping a half-baked self-serve flow loses more pilots than it converts; manual onboarding from a real spa-owner couple is the strongest first impression in the segment. /start is the bridge until the /onboard 5-step wizard proves itself. <strong>Server fn already ported</strong>: <code>submitRefillSetupIntent</code> at <code>src/server/refill-setup.functions.ts</code> writes to <code>csv_scanner_leads</code> with intent-attribution (reuses the prior /scan row by email if it exists, attaching the setup-intent fields rather than creating a parallel record &mdash; one lead per spa). <strong>Cleave changes during port</strong> (same pattern as v1.12 /story): dropped <code>useShell()</code> + <code>brandFor()</code> shell-discriminator, inlined static <code>brand</code> import; translated all slate-*/emerald-NNN/amber-NNN/rose-NNN Tailwind generics to brand tokens (ink, ink-soft, ink-faint, emerald, emerald-soft, amber, amber-soft, rose, rule, paper) per v1.10-v1.11 brand-coherence work; flipped dark CTA from bg-slate-900 to bg-emerald matching v1.11 sweep; flipped the success-state checkmark badge from bg-emerald-500 to bg-emerald; softened card radii rounded-3xl &rarr; rounded-xl per v1.10 polish; required-asterisks use <code>text-rose</code> (brand crimson) instead of <code>text-rose-600</code>. <strong>Critically NOT changed</strong>: form fields, scheduler list (25 options preserved verbatim), success copy (&lsquo;Got it. We&rsquo;ll be in touch within 24 hours&rsquo;), pricing footnote (&lsquo;Refill is free until we actually recover revenue for you. 12% of recovered, then.&rsquo;), all messaging beats intact. <strong>Cross-references that now resolve</strong>: every Karen cold-email CTA pointing at <code>getrefill.app/start</code>, /scan&rsquo;s &lsquo;Set up Refill&rsquo; downstream CTA, /story&rsquo;s &lsquo;Ready when you are&rsquo; scan card. Touched: <code>src/routes/start.tsx</code> (new file, ~310 lines), <code>src/lib/changelog.ts</code> (this entry).",
